Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,How will Qatar’s Father Emir be remembered?,How will Qatar’s Father Emir be remembered?,"How will Qatar’s Father Emir be remembered? Former Emir Sheikh Hamad Bin Khalifa Al Thani has died The man known in Qatar as the Father Emir has died at the age of 74. Sheikh Hamad Bin Khalifa Al Thani ruled from 1995 until 2013, when he stepped aside voluntarily and transferred power to his son. During his reign, Qatar’s economy expanded on an unprecedented scale. His vision set the stage for the nation to emerge as a player in the Gulf region and beyond. Sheikh Hamad is credited with overseeing the deep transformations that shaped Qatar for the past three decades. What lessons will be learned from his legacy? Presenter:Scott McLean Guests: Ibrahim Al Ibrahim – Former economic adviser at the Office of the Emir of Qatar Andreas Krieg – Associate Professor at the School of Security Studies at King’s College London Patrick Theros – Non-Resident Senior Fellow at the Gulf International Forum and former U.S. ambassador to Qatar Save Share","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:14:13 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/inside-story/2026/7/12/how-will-qatars-father-emir-be-remembered?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:02
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Former Spain PM criticised for ‘xenophobic’ remark on French World Cup team,Former Spain PM criticised for ‘xenophobic’ remark on French World Cup team,"Former Spain PM criticised for ‘xenophobic’ remark on French World Cup team Mariano Rajoy condemned for opinion piece on Spanish website El Debate ahead of World Cup semifinal. Save Share Spain’s conservative former prime minister Mariano Rajoy is facing criticism at home and in neighbouring France after saying their national football team had “no French players”. The comment, published in an opinion piece in Spanish online news site El Debate on Sunday, came as Spain prepares to face France in a titanic World Cup semifinal on Tuesday. Spain’s current Prime Minister, Pedro Sanchez, condemned the remark as “xenophobic”. “There are those who still measure belonging by surname, place of birth, or skin colour. Others measure it by our roots in a country and our will to contribute to it,” the Socialist leader wrote on X. “Spain belongs to those who love it and work for it. Not to those who shame it with xenophobic statements.” Transport Minister Oscar Puente dismissed Rajoy as a “post-Franco idiot”. French politicians have also lashed out at Rajoy’s comment. Interior Minister Laurent Nunez told French channel BFMTV that it was “absolutely unacceptable”. Communist party leader Fabien Roussel compared Rajoy’s comment to widely criticised remarks by Paraguayan Senator Celeste Amarilla. She said after Paraguay’s elimination by France in the Round of 16 that star player Kylian Mbappe was a “colonised Cameroonian who has really pretended to be French”. “They just can’t stop themselves from slinging this disgusting racism,” said Roussel. Anti-discrimination minister Aurore Berge also denounced the “repeated racist outbursts”. “It’s time they stopped and that sp","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:09:58 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/7/12/spain-ex-pm-criticised-for-xenophobic-remark-on-french-world-cup-team?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:02
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Iran says almost a dozen ‘enemy projectiles’ targeted Qeshm Island,Iran says almost a dozen ‘enemy projectiles’ targeted Qeshm Island,"Iran says almost a dozen ‘enemy projectiles’ targeted Qeshm Island New explosions have been heard in Bandar Abbas and Qeshm Island. Iran says almost a dozen ‘enemy projectiles’ targeted Qeshm Island New explosions have been heard in Bandar Abbas and Qeshm Island as the US carries out a fifth wave of strikes since a ceasefire agreement was signed three weeks ago. Iranian state media says military sites were targeted in Hormozgan province, with Tehran saying it has retaliated against US military assets in the region. Save Share","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:56:26 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/7/12/iran-says-almost-a-dozen-enemy-projectiles-targeted-qeshm-island?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:03
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Nine dead as Russia and Ukraine trade drone and missile salvos,Nine dead as Russia and Ukraine trade drone and missile salvos,"Nine dead as Russia and Ukraine trade drone and missile salvos Ukraine is particularly vulnerable to Russian ballistic missiles due to critical shortage of Patriot munitions. Save Share Russian drones and missiles killed four people in Ukraine overnight, while Ukrainian attacks on Russia and Russian-occupied areas of Ukraine killed five. Three people were killed in Russian attacks on Ukraine’s central Dnipropetrovsk region overnight, including two at an “industrial enterprise” in the city of Kryvyi Rih, regional officials said on Sunday. In the southern city of Kherson, a drone attack killed a 48-year-old, Mayor Yaroslav Shanko reported. Russia has escalated attacks in recent weeks, taking advantage of Ukraine’s critical shortage of munitions for its Patriot air defence system, which has rendered it largely unable to intercept ballistic missiles flying at several times the speed of sound. NATO countries pledged at their summit in Ankara last week to provide more Patriot munitions to Ukraine, and President Donald Trump said he was willing to give Kyiv a license to manufacture the US missiles domestically. At least 25 heads of state dubbed the “Coalition of the Willing” are due to meet in Paris on Monday to discuss how to support Ukraine and pressure Russia to end the war. Meanwhile, Ukrainian strikes on the Russian-occupied town of Enerhodar killed four people and injured four others, Alexei Likhachev, head of the Russian state nuclear corporation Rosatom, said on Sunday. Enerhodar, home to theZaporizhzhianuclear power plant, fell to Russian forces within weeks of Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. A long-range Ukrainian dron","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:53:03 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/12/nine-dead-as-russia-and-ukraine-trade-drone-and-missile-salvos?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:03
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Iraqi PM to meet US President Trump in Washington to deepen strategic ties,Iraqi PM to meet US President Trump in Washington to deepen strategic ties,"Iraqi PM to meet US President Trump in Washington to deepen strategic ties Oil and gas deals are expected ⁠to be signed as part of a broader push ​for economic, trade and investment cooperation. Save Share Iraq’s Prime MinisterAli al-Zaidiis set to visit the United States to meet President Donald Trump in his first international trip since taking office. Zaidi will depart for the week-long visit on Monday, government spokesman Haider al-Aboudi said. During his visit, oil and gas deals are expected ⁠to be signed as part of a broader push for economic, trade, and investment cooperation between the two countries. “The agreements to be signed will include several memorandums of understanding in the oil and gas sector, ‌as Iraq prepares to bring in various US companies that will provide momentum to increase oil production capacity,” al-Aboudi said. He added that the focus of the talks will be on “strengthening economic relations and investments” between Iraq and the US. Al-Zaidi hopes to attract US investment after significant revenue losses caused by the halt in oil exports due to the Iran war and closure of theStrait of Hormuz.The Gulf, which is the only body of water bordering Iraq. Al-Zaidi, who came to power this year, assumed office amid growing US pressure on Baghdad to crack down on corruption and disarm Iran-backed armed groups that havetargetedUS facilities in Iraq. In a move that pleased the US, Iraqi security forcesarresteddozens of prominent politicians, lawmakers and officials in sweeping raids across Baghdad in late June, as part of an unprecedented anticorruption crackdown ordered by al-Zaidi. Relations ⁠between Iraq and the US have ⁠at times been strained","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:48:00 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/12/iraqi-pm-to-meet-us-president-trump-in-washington-to-deepen-strategic-ties?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:03
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,England vs Argentina: Greatest moments before FIFA World Cup semifinal,England vs Argentina: Greatest moments before FIFA World Cup semifinal,"England vs Argentina: Greatest moments before FIFA World Cup semifinal England and Argentina renew their longstanding football rivalry with a World Cup final place at stake. Save Share England against Argentina for a place in the World Cup Final. Do football matches get any bigger? Nearly two centuries of tangled and bloody history and a fierce and bitter on-field rivalry forged over six decades and punctuated by drama, controversy and a sprinkling of magic. It’s hard to overstate the magnitude of Wednesday’s encounter in Atlanta, which will be the first of any kind between the perennial powerhouses in 21 years. An 18-year-old Lionel Messi was suspended for the previous meeting, a friendly in Geneva in 2005, when England came from 2-1 down to win 3-2 late on. This time all eyes will be on the World Cup’s record scorer as he seeks to lead the defending champions back to the final. The footballing roots between the nations run deep. The first recorded match in Argentina was contested by British railway workers in 1867, and famous old clubs such as Newell’s Old Boys and Rosario Central were founded by expatriates, while the names of River Plate and Boca Juniors were influenced by the language. Argentina was the second country after Scotland to face England in a full international at Wembley Stadium, the hosts winning 2-1 in 1951. But the early bonhomie gave way to a bitter rivalry which has been passed on through generations, with the current crop of Argentina fans still singing about England in the stands throughout this World Cup. But where did it all begin? Let’s take a trip down memory lane for the greatest moments in the history of their rivalr","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:31:20 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/7/12/fifa-world-cup-england-vs-argentina-historic-rivalry-greatest-moments-semifinal?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:03
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Why the Iran-US ceasefire is falling apart,Why the Iran-US ceasefire is falling apart,"Why the Iran-US ceasefire is falling apart Iran, US resumed fighting because they don’t see each other as ‘reliable negotiating partners’, says analyst Ali Vaez. Iran and the US have resumed fighting because they don’t see each other as ‘reliable negotiating partners’, says analyst Ali Vaez. Neither Iran nor the United States seems able to deliver a “knockout blow at an acceptable price” to the other side, and both know “they have no choice other than engaging in diplomacy”, but they’re not ready to make uncomfortable concessions, argues Ali Vaez, director of the Iran Project at International Crisis Group. Vaez tells host Steve Clemons that Tehran and Washington are trying to “enforce their own interpretation” of the ceasefire agreement they signed last month. President Trump has become “frustrated” with diplomacy because he’s not seeing “the kind of quick results that he likes to see”, Vaez says. Save Share","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:27:34 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/the-bottom-line/2026/7/12/why-the-iran-us-ceasefire-is-falling-apart?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:04
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Anti-migrant display set alight in Northern Ireland bonfire,Anti-migrant display set alight in Northern Ireland bonfire,"Anti-migrant display set alight in Northern Ireland bonfire The flags of Palestine, Syria, Sudan and Somalia were draped over a huge bonfire tower before it was set alight. Anti-migrant display set alight in Northern Ireland bonfire The flags of Palestine, Syria, Sudan and Somalia were draped over a huge bonfire tower before it was set alight in Northern Ireland. Police have arrested a man over the ‘hate display’ erected as part of an annual celebration. Save Share","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:21:17 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/7/12/anti-migrant-display-set-alight-in-northern-ireland-bonfire?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:04
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Friends turned foes: The split reshaping Senegal,Friends turned foes: The split reshaping Senegal,"Friends turned foes: The split reshaping Senegal Ousmane Sonko reveals what ended his political partnership with the president, sparking a constitutional standoff. Ousmane Sonko reveals what ended his political partnership with the president, sparking a constitutional standoff. Ousmane Sonko, president of Senegal’s National Assembly, reflects on his fractured alliance with President Bassirou Diomaye Faye, the constitutional standoff dividing the country’s leadership and the future of Senegal’s democracy. He also condemns xenophobic violence in South Africa as “painful” and “unworthy of Africa” and says Africa is owed economic reparations for slavery. Save Share","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:21:00 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/talk-to-al-jazeera/2026/7/12/friends-turned-foes-the-split-reshaping-senegal?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:04
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,"Some 30 Malian soldiers killed during Anefis retaking, says army chief","Some 30 Malian soldiers killed during Anefis retaking, says army chief","Some 30 Malian soldiers killed during Anefis retaking, says army chief General Jean Elysee Dao says 60 others also wounded as army retakes key town after nearly a week of fighting. Save Share The Malian army says about 30 troops have been killed and dozens more wounded during an operation to retake the northern town of Anefis from rebels. Tuareg separatistsand fighters from an armed group linked to al-Qaeda captured Anefis in their latest series ofsimultaneous attackson army positions across the country on July 4. On Friday, the army said it had taken control of the town, some 100km (62 miles) from the strategic city of Kidal, after nearly a week of fighting. “I regret the loss of around 30 people, 30 fallen martyrs,” army chief General Jean Elysee Dao told state TV, adding that about 60 were wounded, including some in serious condition. “We also have around 60 wounded, including serious cases,” Dao said. His comments came a day after the Tuareg-led Azawad Liberation Front (FLA) said it had lost some of its best fighters during the battle against the army and its allied Russian paramilitaries, but had inflicted “the heaviest material and human losses in their history in the region”. Military-run Mali has been grappling with asecurity, political and humanitarian crisisfor more than a decade. The al-Qaeda-linked Jama’at Nusrat al-Islam wal-Muslimin controls swaths of rural territory in the country while the FLA seeks to establish an independent state in northern Mali. While often at odds, fighters from the two groups or their predecessors have also partnered on occasion to fight common enemies, namely Mali’s government and its allies. In late April, they ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:01:40 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/12/some-30-malian-soldiers-killed-during-anefis-retaking-says-army-chief?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:04
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,أوروغواي تستنجد بأسطورتها.. هل يملك فورلان وصفة استعادة الهيبة؟,Uruguay calls on its legend...Does Forlan have the recipe to restore prestige?,"Uruguay calls on its legend...Does Forlan have the recipe to restore prestige? After the World Cup disappointment and Bielsa's resignation, the legend Diego Forlan takes over the leadership of the Uruguay national team on a mission of “restoration.” A complex that extends until 2027. The federation is betting on the experience of the 2010 star to restore lost prestige. Save Share The Uruguayan Football Association announced the appointment of former star Diego Forlan as technical director of the national team, succeeding Argentine Marcelo Bielsa. Bielsa resigned from his position after the Uruguayan national team was eliminated from the 2026 World Cup in America, Mexico and Canada in the group stage. Forlan (47 years old), a legendary football star in his country, will face a major challenge in his coaching career, as it is rebuilding the team that entered the World Cup with great ambitions, but left it with one of the worst performances in its history. The Uruguay national team ranked third in the eighth group of the World Cup with two points in the group that included Spain, Cape Verde and Saudi Arabia. It also failed to qualify from the group stage, and the tournament witnessed a great disappointment for Bielsa, who resigned shortly after the end of his team’s journey in the World Cup. The Uruguayan Federation stated in a statement that Forlan's contract will be extended","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:12:51 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/7/13/%d8%a3%d9%88%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%ba%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%8a-%d8%aa%d8%b3%d8%aa%d9%86%d8%ac%d8%af-%d8%a8%d8%a3%d8%b3%d8%b7%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%aa%d9%87%d8%a7-%d9%87%d9%84-%d9%8a%d9%85%d9%84%d9%83?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:08
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,"دان بيرن ""المرفوض صغيرا"".. كيف تحول إلى بطل إنجلترا في مونديال 2026؟","Dan Byrne, ""rejected as a child""... How did he become England's champion in the 2026 World Cup?","Dan Byrne, ""rejected as a child""... How did he become England's champion in the 2026 World Cup? After years of disappointment and low grades, Dan Byrne has become an unlikely hero, leading England to the 2026 World Cup and writing one of the tournament's most inspiring stories. Save Share In a tournament where attention is usually focused on scorers and stars with bright names, English defender Dan Byrne has established himself as a hero of a different kind. The 34-year-old player did not need exceptional goals or skills to steal the spotlight. Rather, he did so with a series of decisive defensive interventions that contributed to leading England to the semi-finals of the World Cup in 2026. While fans follow what he offers today in the largest football forum, his career recalls the story of a player who was abandoned by his childhood club at an early age, before he returned after many years to write one of the most inspiring stories in the tournament, after rebuilding his career step by step until he reached the England team at an age he did not expect. There are many people who can achieve this dream. Byrne's story at the World Cup began with two defensive moments that reduced his value within the England national team. In the Round of 16 match against Mexico, a scissor kick almost landed","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:10:05 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/7/13/%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%86-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%b1%d9%81%d9%88%d8%b6-%d8%b5%d8%ba%d9%8a%d8%b1%d8%a7-%d9%83%d9%8a%d9%81-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%a5%d9%84%d9%89?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:10
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,تحقيق أمريكي: روسيا حولت اليابان إلى وكر للجواسيس,American investigation: Russia turned Japan into a den of spies,"American investigation: Russia turned Japan into a den of spies An American press investigation revealed that Russia is exploiting legal loopholes and smuggling networks in Japan to obtain advanced technology that supports its military industries, through a secret intelligence unit and intermediary companies, despite Western sanctions on Moscow. Save Share A New York Times investigation revealed that Russia succeeded, despite the sanctions imposed on it after the invasion of Ukraine in 2022, in transforming Japan into one of the most important stations for obtaining advanced technology necessary for the continuation of its military industries, benefiting from legal loopholes and complex smuggling networks operating under diplomatic and commercial cover. The investigation says that Tokyo has become a major destination for dozens of Russian intelligence officers who were expelled from Western capitals in recent years, after Europe and the United States tightened the noose on purchases of electronic components, microchips, and equipment used in manufacturing weapons. According to Western intelligence officials, the pivotal element in these operations is a secret unit of Russian military intelligence known as the “Twenty Directorate,” a unit that has not been publicly disclosed before, and which purchases or steals sensitive technology and smuggles it into Russia via a network.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:58:56 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/politics/2026/7/13/%d8%aa%d8%ad%d9%82%d9%8a%d9%82-%d8%a3%d9%85%d8%b1%d9%8a%d9%83%d9%8a-%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%b3%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d8%ad%d9%88%d9%84%d8%aa-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a5%d9%84%d9%89?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:14
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,سرت تحتضن لقاء عسكريا بين الشرق والغرب لمناقشة توحيد الجيش الليبي,Sirte hosts a military meeting between the East and the West to discuss the unification of the Libyan army,"Sirte hosts a military meeting between the East and the West to discuss the unification of the Libyan army The leaders of the Libyan military establishment are seeking to turn the page on the division through a new meeting of the (5+5) committee in Sirte, amid hopes of achieving unification of the army and paving the way for long-awaited political entitlements. Save Share Yesterday, Sunday, a meeting of the Joint Military Committee (5+5) - which includes military leaders from eastern and western Libya - was held in the city of Sirte, east of the country, amid national and international welcome for this step aimed at unifying the divided Libyan army since the fall of Muammar Gaddafi’s regime in 2011. The meeting included the acting Chief of the General Staff, Lieutenant General Salah al-Din al-Namroush, and the Chief of Staff of the General Command, Lieutenant General Khaled Haftar, with the participation of the Deputy Special Representative of the Secretary-General of the United Nations for Political Affairs. Stephanie Khoury, members of the Joint Military Committee, and a number of military leaders. The Libyan Presidential Council in Tripoli welcomed the holding of the joint military committee meeting, considering - in a statement - that this meeting represents an important step that reflects the continuation of national efforts aimed at strengthening military dialogue, in a way that advances the path of unifying the Libyan military institution. The Presidential Council stressed that this path “represents an extension of the efforts","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:36:20 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/7/13/%d8%b3%d8%b1%d8%aa-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d8%aa%d8%b6%d9%86-%d9%84%d9%82%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d8%b9%d8%b3%d9%83%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d8%a8%d9%8a%d9%86-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%82-%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ba%d8%b1%d8%a8?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:16
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,ميركاتو برشلونة.. لابورتا يحسم مصير رافينيا ويضع مهلة نهائية لصفقة ألفاريز,Mercato Barcelona.. Laporta decides Rafinha's fate and sets a deadline for the Alvarez deal,"Mercato Barcelona.. Laporta decides Rafinha's fate and sets a deadline for the Alvarez deal Barcelona president Joan Laporta spoke about the deal for Julian Alvarez, the Atletico Madrid striker, and Karim Adeyemi, the Borussia Dortmund player, as well as the future of Rafinha. Save Share Joan Laporta, president of the Spanish club Barcelona, ​​arrived in Dallas, Texas, to attend the upcoming match between Spain and France, in the semi-finals of the FIFA World Cup, tomorrow, Tuesday. The Barcelona president spoke to the media who were waiting for him at his residence in the United States, and spoke about many matters regarding Julian Alvarez, the Atletico Madrid striker, and Karim Adeyemi, the Borussia Dortmund player, and also the future of the team’s star Rafinha. Laporta confirmed in statements reported by the Catalan newspaper Mundo Deportivo: “Rafinha is staying with us. There is no intention of dispensing with him. He is a mainstay after supporting the attack with the Anthony Gordon and Adeyemi deals, and that does not mean allowing his departure.” He added: “Unfortunately, Rafinha was not able to give his best in the final stages of the Spanish League, the Champions League and the Spanish King’s Cup last season, so the results would have been very different with his presence.”","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:34:26 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/7/13/%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%b4%d9%84%d9%88%d9%86%d8%a9-%d9%84%d8%a7%d8%a8%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%aa%d8%a7-%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%81%d9%8a%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a7?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:17
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,السودان.. حكم بالإعدام على حميدتي ومجلس الدفاع يرحب بجهود الوساطة,"Sudan.. Hemedti was sentenced to death, and the Defense Council welcomes mediation efforts","Sudan.. Hemedti was sentenced to death, and the Defense Council welcomes mediation efforts Efforts to end the war in Sudan continue with the government declaring its openness to peace initiatives, while the United Nations is sounding the alarm, warning that malnutrition threatens the lives of hundreds of thousands of children. Save Share The Sudanese Security and Defense Council affirmed the government’s openness to any initiatives that would preserve the country’s unity, sovereignty, and territorial integrity, while a Sudanese court issued a death sentence in absentia for the commander of the Rapid Support Forces, Muhammad Hamdan Dagalo (Hemedti). This announcement comes after the regular meeting of the Council, which was held yesterday, Sunday. It is the highest security body in Sudan and is headed by the President of the Sudanese Sovereignty Council, Abdel Fattah Al-Burhan. Its membership includes members of the Sovereignty Council, the Prime Minister, and the Ministers of Finance, Defense, Interior, and Justice, and is specialized in discussing national security issues. In a statement, the Council welcomed the mediation efforts aimed at ending the conflict in Sudan, confirming - at the same time - its submission in response to an American proposal for a road map to stop the war, without revealing its details. The United States had proposed a 90-day humanitarian truce between the army and the Rapid Support Forces, followed by the start of security arrangements in preparation for reaching a solution.","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:51:39 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/7/13/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d9%88%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%ad%d9%83%d9%85-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a5%d8%b9%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%85-%d8%b9%d9%84%d9%89-%d8%ad%d9%85%d9%8a%d8%af%d8%aa%d9%8a-%d9%88%d9%85%d8%ac%d9%84%d8%b3?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:18
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,أسطورة الكاميرون يدافع عنه.. لماذا لا يحظى مبابي بتقدير كامل في فرنسا؟,The Cameroon legend defends him.. Why is Mbappe not fully appreciated in France?,"The Cameroon legend defends him.. Why is Mbappe not fully appreciated in France? The constant criticism of Kylian Mbappe puts the standards of sports appreciation in France to the test, especially since the player does not stop breaking records and consolidating his position as an icon of his generation. Save Share Cameroonian football legend, Samuel Eto'o, expressed his extreme astonishment at the intensity of the criticism faced by French national team captain Kylian Mbappe among the fans in his country, despite his career full of unprecedented achievements and records. In statements made exclusively to Le Parisien newspaper, Eto'o criticized the lack of proper appreciation for what Mbappe (27 years old) offers, stressing that the player, who won the 2018 World Cup title and was runner-up in the 2022 edition, in addition to being the second all-time top scorer in the World Cup, deserves treatment worthy of the great legends of the game. The President of the Cameroonian Football Association pointed out that Mbappe is experiencing a state of “continuous testing” in France, where he is always asked to prove his worth despite the stability of his technical level and the records he has achieved. Eto'o stressed that there is an urgent need for the sports community in France to realize the magnitude of the ""historic gain"" represented by the presence of a B player","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:46:27 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/7/13/%d8%a3%d8%b3%d8%b7%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%83%d8%a7%d9%85%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%88%d9%86-%d9%8a%d8%af%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%b9-%d8%b9%d9%86%d9%87-%d9%84%d9%85%d8%a7%d8%b0%d8%a7-%d9%84%d8%a7?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:19
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,سينر يتغلب على زفيريف ويحتفظ بلقب بطولة ويمبلدون للتنس,Sinner defeats Zverev to retain his Wimbledon title,"Sinner defeats Zverev to retain his Wimbledon title Italian player Jannik Sinner won his fifth major championship title, confirming his absolute dominance over his generation and expanding his special bond against Zverev after achieving his tenth successive victory over him. Save Share Jannik Sinner maintained his title at the Wimbledon Tennis Championships by defeating Alexander Zverev with a score of 6-7, 7-6, 6-3, 6-4 in the final match on Sunday, thus winning his fifth major championship title and extending his advantage over the German player to 10 consecutive victories. With this victory, Sinner joined a rare elite of players, as he became the tenth in the professional era to ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠successfully defend the title, which strengthened his position as one of the dominant players of his generation, while he seeks to chase his great rival Carlos Alcaraz, who has won seven major championship titles. “Honestly, there is no better place to play tennis than this,” Sinner said while holding the Challenge Cup. “I am standing here. You can feel the tension on Sunday morning when you wake up, because you realize that this is a very special day, and you never know how many times you will be able to come back here. So, I never take anything for granted.” He added: “I played in front of...","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:17:57 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/7/13/%d9%88%d9%8a%d9%85%d8%a8%d9%84%d8%af%d9%88%d9%86-%d8%b3%d9%8a%d9%86%d8%b1-%d9%84%d9%82%d8%a8-%d8%b2%d9%81%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%8a%d9%81?traffic_source=rss,2026-07-13 01:24:20
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,صحف أمريكية وبريطانية: مؤسس قطر الحديثة وإرث من الدبلوماسية والقوة الناعمة,American and British newspapers: The founder of modern Qatar and a legacy of diplomacy and soft power,"American and British newspapers: The founder of modern Qatar and a legacy of diplomacy and soft power Qatar invited Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, the architect of its modern renaissance, who transformed it into a global economic, diplomatic and media power, based on investing gas wealth, building soft power, and consolidating its role as an influential mediator. Save Share With the departure of the Father Emir, Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, Qatar bid farewell to a prominent leader who reshaped the features of the Gulf state during the past three decades, after he led an unprecedented transformation that transferred the country from a small country dependent on its natural resources to an influential player in politics, economics, and media at the global level. Western press reports agree that Sheikh Hamad (1952-2026), who assumed power in 1995, deserves to be described as “the founder of modern Qatar,” as his name was associated with launching a comprehensive project to modernize the state, diversify its tools of influence, and employ its gas wealth to build a presence that far exceeds its geographic and demographic size. A report in the New York Times newspaper stated that Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, since assuming the reins of power, had brought about a radical transformation that made Qatar a more independent and influential country, before he voluntarily handed over power to his son, Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani, in 2013. Investment in natural gas was the cornerstone of this transformation.","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:57:42 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/politics/2026/7/13/%d8%b5%d8%ad%d9%81-%d8%a3%d9%85%d8%b1%d9%8a%d9%83%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%88%d8%a8%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%b7%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%85%d8%a4%d8%b3%d8%b3-%d9%82%d8%b7%d8%b1?t