Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Выявлена скрытая причина повышенного риска болезни Альцгеймера,Hidden cause of increased risk of Alzheimer's disease identified,"Hidden cause of increased risk of Alzheimer's disease identified Advertisement A chemical released when car tires wear out may increase the risk of developing Alzheimer's disease. This conclusion was reached by Chinese scientists who for the first time studied in detail the possible effects of this pollutant on brain cells. The results of the study were published in the journal Open Medicine. We are talking about the compound 6PPD-quinone (6PPD-Q). It is formed when the additive 6PPD, which protects tires from cracking, reacts with ozone. This substance has previously been found in water, soil, and even in human biological samples, which indicates that people are in constant contact with it. 6PPD-Q is also known to be able to enter the brain of animals and cause cell damage. In the new work, the researchers used machine learning methods, genetic data analysis and molecular modeling.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:01:47 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/vyyavlena-skrytaya-prichina-povyshennogo-riska-bolezni-altsgeymera/,2026-07-13 01:25:54
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Появились подробности о диалоге ЕС с Россией по Украине,Details have emerged about the EU's dialogue with Russia on Ukraine,"Details have emerged about the EU's dialogue with Russia on Ukraine Advertisement Details have emerged about a possible dialogue between the European Union (EU) and Russia to resolve the situation in Ukraine. Izvestia writes about this with reference to a European diplomatic source. According to the publication, the European Union is open to dialogue, but has not been able to approach the stage of launching official negotiations. No specific decision on the format was made. “We are not yet at the stage of launching such negotiations. Whatever the future format, the participation of Europeans in the process of resolving the situation in Ukraine is inevitable,” the interlocutor added. Earlier, Switzerland expressed its readiness to become a platform for a new round of negotiations to resolve the Russian-Ukrainian conflict.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:51:05 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/poyavilis-podrobnosti-o-dialoge-es-s-rossiey-po-ukraine/,2026-07-13 01:25:56
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Число уничтоженных за неделю над Россией украинских БПЛА подсчитали,The number of Ukrainian UAVs destroyed over Russia in a week has been calculated,"The number of Ukrainian UAVs destroyed over Russia in a week has been calculated Advertising Air defense systems (air defense) intercepted and shot down 4,830 Ukrainian unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) in the skies over Russia over the past week. The number of destroyed targets was calculated by RIA Novosti based on data from the Russian Ministry of Defense. Most of the UAVs were shot down on July 8 and 10. These days, air defense systems shot down 903 and 821 drones, respectively. Most of the attacks occurred in the European part of Russia, the agency notes. On July 12, it was reported that Ukraine launched about 300 drones in Moscow in one day—this attack became one of the largest.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:47:06 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/chislo-unichtozhennyh-za-nedelyu-nad-rossiey-ukrainskih-bpla-podschitali/,2026-07-13 01:25:58
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,США сбили крылатую ракету и беспилотник Ирана,US shoots down Iranian cruise missile and drone,"US shoots down Iranian cruise missile and drone Advertisement The US military intercepted and destroyed an Iranian drone and cruise missile launched towards the Strait of Hormuz. Tim Hawkins, a spokesman for the US Central Command (CENTCOM), told CNN about this. According to him, the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) opened fire about an hour ago in the direction of the channel used by commercial vessels. In response, US forces successfully hit both the cruise missile and the unmanned aerial vehicle. Earlier, on July 12, the US Central Command (CENTCOM) announced its readiness to independently ensure freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, contrary to Iran’s statement about its closure.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:42:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/ssha-sbili-krylatuyu-raketu-i-bespilotnik-irana/,2026-07-13 01:26:00
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Назван автор решения об отмене дисквалификации американского футболиста,The author of the decision to lift the disqualification of an American football player has been named,"The author of the decision to lift the disqualification of an American football player has been named Advertisement The author of the decision to overturn the disqualification of American football player Falorin Balogun has been named. The Times reports this. He became the head of the FIFA Disciplinary Committee, Mohammad Al-Kamali from the United Arab Emirates (UAE). It is noted that he made this decision without the knowledge of the other seventeen members of the committee. In the 1/16 finals of the 2026 World Cup with Bosnia and Herzegovina (2:0), Balogun received a red card for a foul on defender Tarik Muharemovic. The forward had to miss the match with Belgium. “In accordance with Article 27 of the FIFA Disciplinary Code, the one-match suspension is replaced by a probationary period of one year,” FIFA decided. Balogun started in the World Cup Round of 16 match and was substituted in the 92nd minute. The Belgians defeated the USA with a score of 4:1.","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:33:02 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/nazvan-avtor-resheniya-ob-otmene-diskvalifikatsii-amerikanskogo-futbolista/,2026-07-13 01:26:02
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,The Times рассказала о подготовке Финляндии к войне с Россией,The Times spoke about Finland's preparations for war with Russia,"The Times spoke about Finland's preparations for war with Russia Advertising Near Helsinki, 5.5 thousand objects have been opened that can be used as bomb shelters, their capacity is estimated at one million people. The British newspaper The Times spoke about Finland's preparations for war with Russia. It is noted that these facilities function as swimming pools, saunas, gyms, playgrounds, skate parks and concert halls. Moreover, they are located underground and are also equipped with explosion-proof doors and autonomous power supplies. It is emphasized that the conversion of complexes from civilian to shelter will take less than a day. “Officials and politicians from around the world are visiting Helsinki to learn more about its vast underground labyrinth, including representatives of the British Ministry of Defense and (Ukrainian leader Volodymyr) Zelensky,” it says","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:18:32 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/the-times-rasskazala-o-podgotovke-finlyandii-k-voyne-s-rossiey/,2026-07-13 01:26:04
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В России раскрыли причину глубокого кризиса в ОБСЕ,"In Russia, the cause of the deep crisis in the OSCE has been revealed","In Russia, the cause of the deep crisis in the OSCE has been revealed Advertising Director of the Department of European Problems of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MFA) of Russia Vladislav Maslennikov, in a conversation with RIA Novosti, revealed the cause of the deep crisis in the Organization for Security and Cooperation in Europe (OSCE). “The negativity in relation to the OSCE is associated with the desire of the EU and NATO to implement its own exclusively narrow-bloc interests through the Vienna platform, which ultimately drove the Organization into the current state of deep crisis,” Maslennikov said. Maslennikov emphasized that such actions do not cancel the obligations of states to pay annual contributions to the Free Budget of the organization. In addition, the budget adopted for the current year meets Russia's requirements. Earlier, the Permanent Representative of Russia to the OSCE, Mmitry Polyansky, spoke about the attitude of the organization towards the Russian delegation","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:18:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/07/13/v-rossii-raskryli-prichinu-glubokogo-krizisa-v-obse/,2026-07-13 01:26:06
