Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,"Three wives, 24 children and $300 million ‘floating palace’: Meet Qatar’s former ruler Sheikh Hamad who died today","Three wives, 24 children and $300 million ‘floating palace’: Meet Qatar’s former ruler Sheikh Hamad who died today","Three wives, 24 children and $300 million ‘floating palace’: Meet Qatar’s former ruler Sheikh Hamad who died today Sheikh Hamad’s personal wealth placed him among the richest leaders in the world’s royal circles. The bureau represents a collective of experienced journalists, editors, and correspondents who work across television, digital, and social platforms to deliver timely, accurate, and wide-ranging news coverage. Zee Media Bureau's coverage spans politics, business, economy, technology, health, entertainment, and global affairs. The bureau follows a collaborative newsroom model, where stories are researched, verified, and published by a team. This ensures speed, editorial consistency, and adherence to journalistic standards, particularly for breaking news and developing stories. New Delhi:Qatar’s former Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, who died on Sunday (July 12) at the age of 74, was known as the leader who transformed the small Gulf nation into one of the world’s richest countries. His political decisions, economic policies and diplomatic moves strengthened Qatar’s standing in the world. Beyond his role as a ruler, Sheikh Hamad was also known for his lavish lifestyle, vast wealth and royal possessions that matched the scale of his country’s prosperity. According to Qatar News Agency (QNA), he passed away after a life that saw him turn Qatar into a major economic and political player. During his rule, the country increased its influence through its natural gas resources, international investments and diplomatic initiatives. Sheikh Hamad’s personal wealth placed him among the richest leaders in the world’s royal circles. Forbes estimated the private wealth of Britain’s l","Sunday, July 12, 2026, 19:09  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/three-wives-24-children-and-300-million-floating-palace-meet-qatar-s-former-ruler-sheikh-hamad-who-died-today-3060635.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,"Black mask, cap & Khamenei funeral: Who was the man in front row? Identity revealed","Black mask, cap & Khamenei funeral: Who was the man in front row? Identity revealed","Black mask, cap & Khamenei funeral: Who was the man in front row? Identity revealed Wearing a black face mask and a black baseball cap, the man was seen among senior leaders during the funeral ceremony. His appearance became a subject of speculation, with many believing he could be incumbent Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei. The bureau represents a collective of experienced journalists, editors, and correspondents who work across television, digital, and social platforms to deliver timely, accurate, and wide-ranging news coverage. Zee Media Bureau's coverage spans politics, business, economy, technology, health, entertainment, and global affairs. The bureau follows a collaborative newsroom model, where stories are researched, verified, and published by a team. This ensures speed, editorial consistency, and adherence to journalistic standards, particularly for breaking news and developing stories. Tehran:The identity of the masked man seen sitting in the front row during the funeral prayers of Iran’s late Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei has been revealed. According to Iranian media, he has been identified as Mohammad Javad Khamenei, the eldest grandson of the former leader. Wearing a black face mask and a black baseball cap, the man was seen among senior leaders during the funeral ceremony. His appearance became a subject of speculation, with many believing he could be incumbent Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei. However, Iran International reported that the masked mourner was Mohammad Javad Khamenei, the son of Mostafa Khamenei, Ali Khamenei’s eldest son. According to the report, Javad suffered severe facial burns and other injuries during US and Israeli airstrikes on February 28, in which Ayatollah Khamenei was killed. The purported injuries, according to the report, led him to cover his fac","Sunday, July 12, 2026, 18:30  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/black-mask-cap-khamenei-funeral-who-was-the-man-in-front-row-identity-revealed-3060632.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Zee News,India (Right Wing),en,Vietnam detains speedboat captain after 15 Indian tourists die in Phu Quoc tragedy,Vietnam detains speedboat captain after 15 Indian tourists die in Phu Quoc tragedy,"Vietnam detains speedboat captain after 15 Indian tourists die in Phu Quoc tragedy Fifteen Indian tourists were killed after a speedboat reportedly malfunctioned and overturned during an island-hopping tour near Phu Quoc Island in Vietnam. Subhrajit is a journalist with over three years of newsroom experience, covering national and international geopolitics with a sharp focus on India–China–Pakistan affairs. He has spent more than two years with India’s largest television news agency, ANI, and over a year with DD News. He holds a Master’s degree in Mass Communication. He can be reached atsubhrajit.roy@india.com Vietnamese authorities have detained the captain of a speedboat that capsized near Phu Quoc Island, killing 15 Indian tourists. The accident happened during an island-hopping tour on Saturday. Vietnam's Prime Minister has ordered an urgent investigation into the tragedy. The vessel was carrying 32 Indian tourists and four Vietnamese crew members when it reportedly overturned during the trip Also Read:India condemns attack on commercial vessel off Oman's coast; calls for de-escalation in region The captain was identified as Nguyen Hong Hai, 57. He is being investigated for alleged violations of waterway transport safety regulations, according to state media reports. Fifteen Indian tourists were killed after a speedboat carrying 32 Indian tourists and four Vietnamese crew members capsized during an island-hopping tour near Phu Quoc Island in Vietnam. Preliminary information indicated that 10 of the 15 victims were from Tamil Nadu. Authorities said 21 people were rescued. The accident occurred at around 1 PM on Saturday. The speedboat, registered as AG-26751 and operated by Ocean Pearl Island Co, reportedly","Sunday, July 12, 2026, 18:13  +0530",https://zeenews.india.com/world/vietnam-detains-captain-phu-quoc-boat-tragedy-15-indians-dead-3060602.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,'Liars': Laura Loomer claims Mitch McConnell's hospital photo is AI-generated,'Liars': Laura Loomer claims Mitch McConnell's hospital photo is AI-generated,"'Liars': Laura Loomer claims Mitch McConnell's hospital photo is AI-generated Mitch McConnell revealed a fall led to his hospitalization, but his statement photo has sparked online claims that it looks ‘AI generated.’ US senatorMitch McConnell on Sunday revealed for the first time that a fall led to his hospitalization, breaking the silence about the Kentucky Republican's condition after weeks of mounting speculation about his health. McConnell, 84, said in a statement that he has undergone a battery of tests as doctors try to determine what led to his fall. The statement included a smiling picture of McConnell with his wife, Elaine Chao, a tacit response to speculation online that he had died or was incapacitated. McConnell held a copy of Sunday's Washington Post sports section in his hand. However, the photo has drawn scrutiny online. Laura Loomer posted, “Why does the text on the newspaper McConnell's staff claim he's holding look AI generated? The text is blurry and the tag on his shirt is blurred. Also, if he's in the hospital, why is there no IV connected to him to monitor his health? This is such bullshit. His staff are liars."" She also wrote, “There's no way Mitch McConnell wrote that essay.” Also Read: 'Mitch McConnell hospital photo taken today': Washington Post's sports section in Senator's hands emerges as 'proof' Kylie Jane Kremer wrote, “The photo itself raises additional questions. The newspaper text is too blurry to independently verify the date or publication, so it does not establish when the photo was actually taken.” Another user wrote, “Looks more like a nursing home setting than being an inpatient at a hospital.” Someone else posted, “I absolutely love that Ai is goin","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:53:39 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/liars-laura-loomer-claims-mitch-mcconnells-hospital-photo-is-aigenerated-101783898876995.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Nolan Wells' death sparks protests in Ocean Springs, Mississippi as hundreds demand answers; videos surface","Nolan Wells' death sparks protests in Ocean Springs, Mississippi as hundreds demand answers; videos surface","Nolan Wells' death sparks protests in Ocean Springs, Mississippi as hundreds demand answers; videos surface A protest was held after the death of Nolan Wells, an 18-year-old from Ocean Springs, Mississippi, with demonstrators demanding more transparency in the case. A protest was held on Saturday, July 11, after the death ofNolan Xavier Wells, an 18-year-old from Ocean Springs, Mississippi, with demonstrators demanding more transparency in the case. Wells was reportedly found dead in the water on the northwest end of Horn Island on Monday morning, July 6. Wells went missing on July 4 after taking a boat to the island with friends. Thesearch for the teen was called offafter abody was foundby a park ranger on Monday, July 6. On Saturday, more than 100 protesters gathered to demand answers, according to NBC News. Speculation about the circumstances of his death continues to grow. Several advocacy groups have now called for a full and transparent investigation. Videos of the protests have surfaced on X. “Theres currently a peaceful protest in Ocean Springs in honor of Nolan Wells. I’m here live:,”one video is captioned. “Protest for Nolan Wells through the streets of downtown Ocean Springs, Mississippi,” readsanother video. Well’s family joined attorneyBen Crumpand the Rev. Al Sharpton in New York for a press conference on Friday, July 10, and for a “full, transparent and urgent investigation” into his death. Crump said in a recent interview with Don Lemon that Wells’ body was being flown to Washington, D.C., for a medical examiner to study. He added that the second autopsy will find out ""if he had any physical injuries to his body beyond drowning."" Crump told Lemon that his investigation is still in very early stages and he does not yet kno","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:45:23 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/nolan-wells-death-sparks-protests-in-ocean-springs-mississippi-as-hundreds-demand-answers-videos-surface-101783901182355.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Cyclospora outbreak spreads to 32 states: Symptoms and how to protect yourself,Cyclospora outbreak spreads to 32 states: Symptoms and how to protect yourself,"Cyclospora outbreak spreads to 32 states: Symptoms and how to protect yourself A fast-spreading stomach parasite has sickened thousands of people across more than 30 US states. Thousands of people across theUnited Stateshave been infected with cyclosporiasis, an intestinal illness caused by the Cyclospora parasite, as health officials continue to investigate the source of the outbreak. As per anABC News, cases of cyclosporiasis, an intestinal infection caused by a parasite are currently being reported in nearly three dozen states. As of Friday, at least 2,944 cases have been reported in 32 states, according to data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and state health departments. According to the CDC, the true number of people sick with cyclosporiasis is likely higher than the reported figure because some people recover without medical care and are not tested for the parasite. The parasite usually spreads through food or water contaminated with feces. The most common symptom of cyclosporiasis is watery diarrhea “with frequent and sometimes explosive bowel movements,” according to the CDC. Other symptoms may include nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain or bloating. As perFox Weather, the illness also commonly triggers stomach cramps or pain, bloating and increased gas. The time between becoming infected and showing symptoms is typically about one week but can range from two days to two weeks. As perNPR, those sickened with the disease have ranged in age from 5 to 88 years old. Foodborne outbreaks of cyclosporiasis have been linked to various types of imported fresh produce, such as raspberries, basil, snow peas, mesclun lettuce and ","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 04:50:11 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/cyclospora-outbreak-spreads-to-32-states-symptoms-and-how-to-protect-yourself-101783895128616.html,2026-07-13 01:29:39
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,'Mitch McConnell hospital photo taken today': Washington Post's sports section in Senator's hands emerges as 'proof','Mitch McConnell hospital photo taken today': Washington Post's sports section in Senator's hands emerges as 'proof',"'Mitch McConnell hospital photo taken today': Washington Post's sports section in Senator's hands emerges as 'proof' Mitch McConnell's office shared a hospital photo as proof he's alive, but conspiracy theories persisted despite a dated Washington Post visible in his hands. Mitch McConnell's office has always maintained that the 84-year-old has been recovering in the hospital after his June 12 hospitalization. But the MAGA contingent on social media has refused to believe it, demanding thatproofof life be provided. On Sunday afternoon, amid renewed interest in the Kentucky Senator's health after the death of Sen. Lindsey Graham of South Carolina late on Saturday, Mitch McConnell's office provided the much-awaited proof that the Senator is alive. It came in the form of a photo of Senator McConnell in ahospitalbed along with his wife, Elaine Chao. But the conspiracy theorists were not convinced, with many claiming that the photo of Senator McConnell and Elaine Chao is AI-generated. But a key detail in the photo challenged those claims. Also read:Mitch McConnell update: Lindsey Graham's death sparks renewed interest in Kentucky Senator's health; ‘where is he?’ Amid claims that the photo is fake, users on social media were quick to notice a key detail: the newspaper that Lindsey Graham held in his hands on the hospital bed. The 84-year-old was seen holding the front page of theWashington Post'sSports section for today, i.e. July 12. In the flap of the newspaper that McConnell held, the photo of the new Washington Nationals draftee from the Texas A&M Aggies, Chris Hacopian could be seen. A part of Hacopian's face and the column just beside it on Linda Nosková's Wimbledon women's title win on Saturday. Along with the photo, the office of Senator Mitch","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 04:03:31 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/mitch-mcconnell-hospital-photo-taken-today-washington-posts-sports-section-in-senators-hands-emerges-as-proof-101783894436441.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Mitch McConnell gives health update, shares photo from hospital; 'Was briefly unconscious, had mild pneumonia'","Mitch McConnell gives health update, shares photo from hospital; 'Was briefly unconscious, had mild pneumonia'","Mitch McConnell gives health update, shares photo from hospital; 'Was briefly unconscious, had mild pneumonia' After four weeks away, Mitch McConnell finally revealed what happened during the health scare that landed him in hospital. After weeks of questions about his health and absence from the Senate, Mitch McConnell has finally spoken publicly about the medical incident that led to his hospitalization. The 84-year-oldRepublicansenator from Kentucky shared his first public photo since stepping away from Washington, appearing alongside his wife, former Transportation Secretary Elaine Chao. In a statement addressed to Kentucky residents, McConnell revealed that he briefly lost consciousness after a fall last month and was taken to the hospital. He also disclosed that doctors later diagnosed him with a mild case of pneumonia while he was receiving treatment. According toMcConnell, doctors ruled out several serious conditions that many people had feared could be behind his hospitalization. He said medical tests showed he had not suffered a stroke, heart attack, concussion, tumor or hemorrhage. The senator added that he continues to undergo testing as doctors work to determine exactly what caused him to lose consciousness. The update was released four weeks after he disappeared from public view, according to the Daily Mail. In his message, McConnell thankedKentuckiansfor their support while acknowledging that many had been seeking answers about his health. “To my fellow Kentuckians,” he wrote, “when you elected me to a seventh term and made me our Commonwealth's longest serving Senator, you did so trusting that I'd keep showing up to fight for you every day.” Also Read:Mitch McConnell update: Lindsey Graham'","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:28:14 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/mitch-mcconnell-gives-health-update-shares-photo-from-hospital-was-briefly-unconscious-had-mild-pneumonia-101783893114080.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Did Candace Owens know about Lindsey Graham's death? Old remarks resurface amid 'setup' claims,Did Candace Owens know about Lindsey Graham's death? Old remarks resurface amid 'setup' claims,"Did Candace Owens know about Lindsey Graham's death? Old remarks resurface amid 'setup' claims Candace Owens’ resurfaced comments have added a new twist to the online conversation following Lindsey Graham’s death. Senator Lindsey Graham died at the age of 71 on July 11 after what his office described as a “brief and sudden illness.” Reports published after his death said emergency responders were called after he experienced chest pains, and some reports linked the incident to a possible cardiac arrest. His death came just hours after he returned from a visit to Ukraine, where he met President Volodymyr Zelenskyy and discussed sanctions on Russia, air defense support and Ukraine’s defense industry. Almost immediately, social media users began connecting Graham’s death to past comments made by conservative commentator Candace Owens. While no evidence has been presented to support any wrongdoing, several posts on X fueled speculation, turning an already high-profile death into a political talking point online. Owens has been one of Graham’s loudest critics for years, especially on foreign policy. During a recent appearance on Russian state media, she said, “I’m not dealing with congress. I’m not dealing with lobbying. I’m not dealing with any of this. I’m not dealing with Lindsey Graham calling for another war.” She has also repeatedly accusedGrahamof being “compromised.” In an August 2025 post, Owens wrote, “In my mind I rate how extreme the blackmail Israel has on each of our politicians must be and with Lindsey you just know it’s terrifyingly so. Lindsey and Corey Booker.” Earlier, in February 2024, she posted, “They have blackmail on Lindsey Graham. Abundantly obvious. Whatever it is,","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:24:31 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/did-candace-owens-know-about-lindsey-grahams-death-old-remarks-resurface-amid-setup-claims-101783883962006.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Why are flags at half-mast today? Trump's big announcement after Sen. Lindsey Graham's sudden death,Why are flags at half-mast today? Trump's big announcement after Sen. Lindsey Graham's sudden death,"Why are flags at half-mast today? Trump's big announcement after Sen. Lindsey Graham's sudden death Following Lindsey Graham's death, President Trump ordered US flags at half-staff nationwide through July 18, 6pm, to honor the late South Carolina senator. On Sunday (July 12), the United States woke up to the news of South Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham's suddendeath. The passing of the 71-year-old left Trump, who considered Graham a ""good friend,"" in shock. So much so that the POTUS announced country-wide mourning for the deceased Senator. Hours after his death, Trump ordered thatnational flagat state buildings across the United States be flown at half-mast till Saturday (July 18) as the nation mourns the death of Senator Lindsey Graham. As a result, many in the US are expected to see flags at half-staff at state buildings and specific private buildings till 6pm local time on July 18, Saturday. Also read:Why did Lindsey Graham never get married? What late senator revealed, ‘The right girl was smart enough not to…’ Trump mourned the death his ""dear friend"" Lindsey Graham in two separate Truth Social Post. In the first post, his first public reaction to the news of Graham's death, Trump remembered Graham as a ""great American patriot."" He announced the seven-day national mourning in a follow-up post. “In honor of the remarkable life and achievements of Senator Lindsey Graham, a dear friend of mine, and a truly great man, who achieved so much for our Country, and his beloved Home State of South Carolina, I am ordering all American Flags throughout the United States lowered to Half Mast until Saturday at 6 p.m.,” Trump wrote. Flags being flown at half-mast is a common practice to mark national mourning. It can be announced in the ","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 03:01:49 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/why-are-flags-at-half-mast-trumps-big-announcement-after-sen-lindsey-grahams-sudden-death-101783890082607.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Who is Ben Shapiro's wife Dr. Mor Shapiro? All about the doctor as couple welcomes fifth child,Who is Ben Shapiro's wife Dr. Mor Shapiro? All about the doctor as couple welcomes fifth child,"Who is Ben Shapiro's wife Dr. Mor Shapiro? All about the doctor as couple welcomes fifth child Ben Shapiro’s fifth child announcement has renewed interest in Mor Shapiro, the doctor who largely stays away from public attention. Ben Shapiro has shared a rare update about his personal life after announcing that he and his wife, Dr. Mor Shapiro, have welcomed their fifth child. The conservative political commentator posted the news on X, writing, “With immeasurable thanks to God, we’re proud to announce the addition of baby number 5 to the Shapiro family this morning.” The announcement drew focus on Mor Shapiro, who has largely stayed out of the public eye despite her husband’s high-profile media career. While Ben Shapiro is known for his political commentary and as a co-founder of The Daily Wire, Mor has built her own career in medicine and has generally kept her family life private. MorShapiro, whose maiden name is Mor Toledano, was born in Herzliya, Israel. She later moved to the United States with her family and pursued a career in medicine. According tothe Sun, Mor Shapiro studied at the University of California, Los Angeles (UCLA) before earning her medical degree from the David Geffen School of Medicine at UCLA. The report also said she has worked in family medicine and was associated with the Family Medicine Residency Program at Kaiser Foundation Hospital in California. Beyond her clinical work, Mor has shown a strong interest in medical ethics and women’s health. She was involved in organizing ethics-related programs during her time at medical school, reflecting her focus on patient care and healthcare education. Unlike her husband, Mor rarely appears in interviews or public events. She has la","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:51:51 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/who-is-ben-shapiros-wife-dr-mor-shapiro-all-about-the-doctor-as-couple-welcomes-fifth-child-101783889004628.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"'Assassination threat': Laura Loomer sounds alarm over Iran LEGO video after Lindsey Graham's death, seeks FBI response","'Assassination threat': Laura Loomer sounds alarm over Iran LEGO video after Lindsey Graham's death, seeks FBI response","'Assassination threat': Laura Loomer sounds alarm over Iran LEGO video after Lindsey Graham's death, seeks FBI response An Iran LEGO video, a checked-off name and Laura Loomer’s FBI appeal have added new questions after Graham’s death. Senator Lindsey Graham’s sudden death has triggered fresh online controversy after conservative activist Laura Loomer shared a LEGO-style video from an Iranian account that appeared to celebrate the South Carolina Republican’s death and mention her by name. Graham died on July 11 at the age of 71 after suffering cardiac arrest following his return from a trip to Ukraine. US authorities have not indicated any evidence of foul play, and available reports point to natural causes. Still, the video drew attention after Loomer claimed it contained a message directed at her and urged federal authorities to take the matter seriously. In a post on X,Loomershared a video published by an account called “Lego Resistance Front,” which claimed Graham had been assassinated. The animation shows a hooded figure entering a mansion at night before a LEGO character resembling Graham collapses. Later, a checklist appears with “Lindsey” marked off and “Laura” listed next. Reacting to the video, Loomer wrote: “BREAKING: An Iranian regime account is now claiming Iran assassinated Senator Lindsey Graham! They just released one of their state sponsored IRGC LEGO propaganda videos showing what is supposed to be an Iranian hiding outside of the Senator’s home late at night and then breaking inside and triggering a cardiac arrest. The video ends with the Senator dying inside an ambulance and a person checking the name ‘Lindsey’ off a checklist. The checklist says ‘Laura’ is next. This is a direct referen","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:51:21 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/assassination-threat-laura-loomer-sounds-alarm-over-iran-lego-video-after-lindsey-grahams-death-seeks-fbi-response-101783891013340.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Lindsey Graham's cause of death revealed amid 'assassination' and 'poisoning' theories: What is an aortic rupture?,Lindsey Graham's cause of death revealed amid 'assassination' and 'poisoning' theories: What is an aortic rupture?,"Lindsey Graham's cause of death revealed amid 'assassination' and 'poisoning' theories: What is an aortic rupture? According to a preliminary finding from the medical examiner, Lindsey Graham died from an aortic rupture caused by hardened arteries. Lindsey Graham, the longtime Republican US senator from South Carolina and a close ally of President Donald Trump, died on Saturday at the age of 71. According to a preliminary finding from the medical examiner,Lindsey Grahamdied from an aortic rupture caused by hardened arteries. An aortic rupture is a life-threatening medical emergency in which the aorta tears or bursts completely. The aorta is the body's largest artery. It carries oxygen-rich blood from the heart to the rest of the body. A rupture can cause severe internal bleeding and can quickly become fatal without immediate treatment. According to Mayo Clinic, aorta rupture is often linked to an aortic aneurysm, a weakened, bulging section of the aorta that can burst. Risk factors include high blood pressure, atherosclerosis, smoking, advanced age, connective tissue disorders, trauma, a family history of aortic disease, and a bicuspid aortic valve. In some cases, sudden physical or emotional stress may trigger a rupture. Common symptoms include sudden, severe ""tearing"" or ripping pain in the chest, upper back, or abdomen, shortness of breath, loss of consciousness, weakness on one side of the body, and signs of shock such as low blood pressure and a rapid pulse. The condition can sometimes be mistaken for aheart attack. According to NBC News, emergency personnel responded to a call for ""cardiac arrest"" at Graham's Capitol Hill home on Saturday night. In a post on X, his office announced his death, saying he died after ","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:50:15 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/lindsey-grahams-cause-of-death-revealed-amid-assassination-and-poisoning-theories-what-is-an-aortic-rupture-101783890842452.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,What was Lindsey Graham's last 'secret' stop? Inside the hidden Ukrainian drone factory he visited before his death,What was Lindsey Graham's last 'secret' stop? Inside the hidden Ukrainian drone factory he visited before his death,"What was Lindsey Graham's last 'secret' stop? Inside the hidden Ukrainian drone factory he visited before his death Just one day before he died, Senator Lindsey Graham secretly toured a Ukrainian drone factory.&nbsp; South CarolinaSenatorLindsey Grahamvisited a secret Ukrainian military drone factory just one day before his sudden death Saturday evening at age 71. The visit came during his trip toUkraine, hours before his office announced his passing from a “brief and sudden illness.” Graham toured a production facility belonging to Ukrainian defense company SkyFall, according to Ukraine Pravda, as cited by theNew York Post. During the visit, he also met Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, along with his House colleague Rep Michael McCaul (R-TX). The plant produces Ukraine's “Vampire” bomber drones, also called “Baba Yaga,” which are capable of carrying explosive charges behind enemy lines. Graham said the US could learn from Ukraine's advances in drone technology, arguing it would be a mistake for America not to work with Ukraine in this area, as per the New York Post. Also Read:Lindsey Graham's final moments: Photos show the senator being wheeled out on a gurney as EMS fought to save him On Friday, Graham also said he hadreached an agreementwith the White House on a Russia sanctions bill that the Trump administration is ready to support. Graham died Saturday night “from a brief and sudden illness,” his office said in a statement, adding that the family “appreciates prayers at this time and asks for privacy during this incredibly difficult period.” Emergency personnel had responded to a call for cardiac arrest at Graham's DC home. Also Read:Was Lindsey Graham assassinated? Putin aide","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:53:10 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/what-was-lindsey-grahams-last-secret-stop-inside-the-hidden-ukrainian-drone-factory-he-visited-before-his-death-101783879522690.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Bangkok fire: At least 27 people killed as blaze breaks out at a pub,Bangkok fire: At least 27 people killed as blaze breaks out at a pub,"Bangkok fire: At least 27 people killed as blaze breaks out at a pub Footage shared online by first responders shows a huge blaze raging and plumes coming out of the front door of the Na Ladprao pub. BANGKOK (AP) — A huge fire engulfed a pub inBangkokearly on Monday morning, killing at least 27 people before firefighters brought the blaze under control, officials said. Footage shared online by first responders shows a huge blaze raging and plumes coming out of the front door of the Na Ladprao pub in the northern part of the Thai capital. People are seen trying to flee as thick black smoke billows into the sky. Rescuers said the fire was reported around midnight. Thailand Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul told reporters at the scene that 27 people died and that several of the injured have been taken to the hospital. He said the cause of the fire is under investigation. Anutin said a musician who was performing at the pub told him that he saw smoke coming out of a circuit breaker near the stage before the power went out, then an explosion was heard and thick smoke quickly filled the place. Many of victims were found at the restrooms, at the back of the pub, Anutin added. Firefighters took about half an hour to bring the fire under control. Photos of the aftermath show charred tables and chairs, and the damaged interior of the pub. Thailand has seen similar tragedies in the past. In 2022,14 people were killed by a fireat a music pub in the eastern part of the country. And more than a decade before that, 66 people were killed and more than 200 injured ina fire during a Jan. 1, 2009New Year’s Eve celebration at the Santika nightclub in Thailand's capital. That blaze was appar","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 01:37:38 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/bangkok-thailand-fire-at-least-27-people-killed-as-blaze-breaks-out-at-a-pub-101783886525670.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Steamboat Springs fire: Smoke seen near Rabbit Ears Pass in National Forest; photos and videos surface,Steamboat Springs fire: Smoke seen near Rabbit Ears Pass in National Forest; photos and videos surface,"Steamboat Springs fire: Smoke seen near Rabbit Ears Pass in National Forest; photos and videos surface Officials are responding after smoke was spotted near Rabbit Ears Pass in the National Forest outside Steamboat Springs. Awildfirehas been reported near Steamboat Springs inColorado. According to Steamboat Springs Fire Rescue (SSFR), SSFR and Dispatch are aware of smoke seen on Rabbit Ears Pass. As per the department, the incident is located in the National Forest and the US Forest Service is responding and will oversee the incident. Here is the video: According to people onsocial media, thefirestarted at 11:45am local times. SSFR thanked everyone who called in to report the smoke and urged people to “stay safe.” Also Read:Summit Fire video: LA wildfire burns over 2,600 acres as evacuations continue, advisory issued: ‘If people feel…’ SSFR's statement: “SSFR and Dispatch are aware of the smoke on Rabbit Ears Pass. The incident is in the National Forest and US Forest Service is responding and will oversee the incident. Thank you to everyone who called it in and please stay safe.” Summit Fire which started on July 11, is still burning in the Antelope Valley community of Llano,California, with officials reporting that forward progress on the blaze has been stopped and containment has increased. According to fire officials, the fire has burned 2,690 acres and is now 15% contained. More than 500 firefighters have battled the blaze since it erupted Friday near Jesus Canyon Road and East Avenue Z. One firefighter suffered minor injuries and is expected to recover. The fire has damaged one residence and destroyed one minor structure, as perABC 7. Evacuation orders have been lifted in bothLos Angelesand","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:28:37 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/steamboat-springs-fire-smoke-seen-near-rabbit-ears-pass-in-national-forest-photos-and-videos-surface-101783882046857.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Mitch McConnell update: Lindsey Graham's death sparks renewed interest in Kentucky Senator's health; ‘where is he?’,Mitch McConnell update: Lindsey Graham's death sparks renewed interest in Kentucky Senator's health; ‘where is he?’,"Mitch McConnell update: Lindsey Graham's death sparks renewed interest in Kentucky Senator's health; ‘where is he?’ Trump called Lindsey Graham's death a blow to the SAVE America Act. It renewed scrutiny over Mitch McConnell's health ahead of key Senate votes. TheRepublican Partymajority in theUS Senatehas been under jeopardy with the absence of Senator Mitch McConnell of Kentucky, who has not been seen in public since his June 12 hospitalization. On Sunday, the GOP was dealt another blow with the death of Senator Lindsey Graham of South Carolina. Graham died after a""sudden illness""following his return from Kyiv, Ukraine, on Saturday, his office said in a statement early Sunday morning. Lindsey Graham's death sparked many conspiracy theories, especially around foreign involvement. While those remain underinvestigation by the FBI, what's real is the compounded hurdle that the GOP will face with pushing Trump's agenda with both Mitch McConnell and Lindsey Graham absent from Senate votes. Even PresidentDonald Trump, as he remembered the late South Carolina Senator Sunday after his death, recalled their conversation about passing the SAVE America Act, which aims to bring sweeping changes in voting eligibility rules. Also read:Mitch McConnell ‘preparing’ to resume Senate duties amid health concerns: Scott Jennings says ‘he was meeting with…’ Speaking to NBC News’s “Meet the Press,” Trump told host Kristen Welker that Graham's death is a ""big blow"" to the passage of the SAVE America Act. “This is a big blow to the SAVE America Act, let me tell you,” Trump said. “He was a worker; he was really a worker. But he sounded great, actually, but he actually said he was tired,"" Trump added. ""But he wanted to pass the SAVE America Act, and I said,","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:16:51 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/mitch-mcconnell-update-lindsey-grahams-death-sparks-renewed-interest-in-kentucky-senators-health-where-is-he-101783879821843.html,2026-07-13 01:29:40
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Eric Trump says ETH is pumping hard: Why Ethereum price is rising today,Eric Trump says ETH is pumping hard: Why Ethereum price is rising today,"Eric Trump says ETH is pumping hard: Why Ethereum price is rising today Eric Trump says ETH is pumping hard as Ethereum climbs above $1,800. Here's why ETH is rising, whale buying, ETF inflows and the $2,000 target. Eric Trump celebrated Ethereum's rally on social media. Eric Trump posted on X, saying, ""ETH is pumping hard! Great to see! Crypto is the future…"", asEthereumcontinued its latest price recovery. Ethereum has climbed back above the key $1,800 level. After spending the last few days above its expected level, ETH started trading around $1,810-$1,819, depending on the exchange, as per the Market data. ETH is up around 1.7%-1.8% in the last 24 hours. Over the past day, Ethereum gained about 1.75% and was hovering near $1,818.76 during the latest update, recorded the Pluang market data. Ethereum remains the world's second-largest cryptocurrency, with market capitalization of about $218 billion, keeping it behind only Bitcoin in thecrypto market. The rally comes after a difficult period. Ethereum had struggled in recent weeks before reclaiming the $1,800 mark, making the latest move an important recovery for investors. However, trading activity is actually falling. Even though prices are rising, Ethereum's 24-hour spot trading volume dropped nearly 12% to around $7.3 billion, showing fewer traders are taking part in the rally. Experts say low trading volume can be a warning sign. Price recoveries that happen while trading activity is falling can be fragile because they may not have enough buying support to continue for long, according to Pluang. Crypto traders saw massive liquidations during the last 24 hours. Across crypto markets, about $111.7 million worth of positions were liqui","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:04:41 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/eric-trump-says-eth-is-pumping-hard-why-ethereum-price-is-rising-today-101783879950432.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Israel elections to be held on October 27, Netanyahu to face tough challenge","Israel elections to be held on October 27, Netanyahu to face tough challenge","Israel elections to be held on October 27, Netanyahu to face tough challenge Netanyahu is already the country's longest-serving prime minister, having served multiple, non-consecutive terms, and has declared his intention to run again. Israel will hold national elections on October 27, the last date allowed by law, its parliament said on Sunday, with the vote widely seen as a referendum on Prime MinisterBenjamin Netanyahu's leadership since the Gaza war erupted. The Knesset, as parliament is known, is set to end its current term on July 17, allowing the ruling coalition to complete a full four-year term for the first time in decades. ""Since the current Knesset is expected to serve its full term and the next general election is already set by law for October 27, with no intention of shortening the legislature's tenure, there is no need to enact a Knesset Dissolution Law in the usual sense,"" parliament said in a statement. Netanyahu, 76, is already the country's longest-serving prime minister, having served multiple, non-consecutive terms, and has declared his intention to run again. He has said he ""intends to win"" the election, setting the stage for what could be the defining contest of his political life. In recent days, his government -- one of the most right-wing coalitions in Israel's history -- has been racing to pass a series of bills in a bid to shore up his alliance and enter the election from a position of strength. Last month, Netanyahu even said that he intended to ""establish a broad national government, not a right-wing, not a left-wing government that depends on Arab parties, but a broad national government"". By reaching across the aisle, Netanyahu appears to be trying to reframe his electoral p","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:03:37 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/israel-elections-to-be-held-on-october-27-netanyahu-to-face-tough-challenge-101783877145995.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Was Lindsey Graham assassinated? Putin aide blames Israel's Mossad amid MAGA's ‘poisoned’ claim; ‘Trump is next…’,Was Lindsey Graham assassinated? Putin aide blames Israel's Mossad amid MAGA's ‘poisoned’ claim; ‘Trump is next…’,"Was Lindsey Graham assassinated? Putin aide blames Israel's Mossad amid MAGA's ‘poisoned’ claim; ‘Trump is next…’ Lindsey Graham's death fueled conspiracy theories, with Putin adviser Alexander Dugin claiming Mossad killed the senator to push Trump into war with Iran. The death ofSouth CarolinaRepublican Senator Lindsey Graham has opened a Pandora's box of conspiracy theories on social media. Leading the charge is far-right influencer Laura Loomer, who has claimed that Iran or Russia ""poisoned"" the Senator, who recently visited Ukraine in an official capacity. The Senator's death came just hours after he had returned from Kyiv. Graham's office said early that he died from a ""brief illness"" on Saturday night. He was 71. Later, his office revealed the Senator'scause of deathas a tear in his aorta due to cardiovascular disease. But the sudden nature of his death has sparked theories and doubts in the public mind, especially about a foreign plot to kill the Senator being at work. So much so,FBI Director Kash Patel announcedlater on Sunday that the agency will investigate the Senator's death. Even as MAGA claim that the Senator was poisoned by either Russia or Iran, a completely different hypothesis has emerged from the Russian side. According to a top advisor of Russia's president Vladimir Putin, Israel's counterintelligence agency Mossad could be behind the death of the 71-year-old Senator. Also read:Lindsey Graham's cause of death revealed amid 'assassination' and 'poisoning' theories: What is an aortic rupture? The Senator, notably, was a close ally of the Israel cause throughout his political career. After his death, Israel PMBenjamin Netanyahuremembered him as a ""good friend"" and said that he already misses Graham. Alexander Dugin, a Russ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:01:21 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/was-lindsey-graham-assassinated-putin-aide-blames-israels-mossad-amid-magas-poisoned-claim-trump-is-next-101783875875101.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Israeli drone strike in Gaza kills 6 people, including 9-year-old girl, say health officials","Israeli drone strike in Gaza kills 6 people, including 9-year-old girl, say health officials","Israeli drone strike in Gaza kills 6 people, including 9-year-old girl, say health officials The Israeli military acknowledged striking the area, saying it targeted “terrorist infrastructure,” without elaborating Israeli fire inGazaon Sunday killed at least six Palestinians, including a 9-year-old girl, and wounded over a dozen others, according to local health officials. A drone strike on a blacksmith shop in Gaza City’s Sabra neighborhood killed at least four Palestinians, according to officials at Shifa hospital, where the casualties were taken. The Israelimilitaryacknowledged striking the area, saying it targeted “terrorist infrastructure,” without elaborating. It later said it struck a Hamas weapon production site. Also Read |Trump Wanted 20,000 Peacekeeping Troops in Gaza. He Is Starting With 10 to 20. Palestinians received an evacuation order from the military following the first strikes. Roughly an hour later, intense airstrikes targeted the same blacksmith shop. The Palestinian Red Crescent Society’s ambulance service said the strikes in Gaza City wounded 14 people. Also on Sunday, Israeli gunfire killed 9-year-old Tala Abu Matar in a displacement camp in central Gaza, according to officials at the Health Ministry. The Israeli military said it was unaware of such an incident. And anIsraelistrike on a displacement tent in southern Gaza’s Khan Younis killed one Palestinian, according to health officials at Nasser hospital, where the body was taken. Israel’s military said it carried out a strike in that area and called it “part of routine activities.” The military said it was not aware of casualties. Israeli strikes have lessened considerably since a ceasefire took effect on Oct","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:58:16 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/israeli-fire-in-gaza-kills-6-people-including-9-year-old-girl-say-health-officials-101783876977863.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Lindsey Graham's final moments: Photos show the senator being wheeled out on a gurney as EMS fought to save him,Lindsey Graham's final moments: Photos show the senator being wheeled out on a gurney as EMS fought to save him,"Lindsey Graham's final moments: Photos show the senator being wheeled out on a gurney as EMS fought to save him Senator Lindsey Graham died suddenly Saturday night, just a day after returning from Ukraine.&nbsp; South CarolinaSenatorLindsey Grahamwho was 71 has died on Saturday night after a “brief and sudden illness,” his office confirmed. Graham, a close Trump ally often called the “Trump Whisperer,” had just returned from a trip toUkrainethe day before hisdeath. “Senator Graham’s family appreciates prayers at this time and asks for privacy during this incredibly difficult period,” the statement said. As per theIndependent, US media reported that emergency personnel had responded to reports of a cardiac arrest at Graham's Washington home Saturday night. According toTMZ, emergency medical workers responded to Graham's Washington, DC, home on Saturday night after reports of a medical emergency. Exclusive photos published by the outlet showed the South Carolina senator being wheeled out of his residence on a gurney while paramedics gave him emergency treatment. Graham appeared to be intubated as paramedics lifted him into an ambulance, according to TMZ. Here are the photos: Also Read:Lindsey Graham dies. How South Carolina's small-town boy rose to become Trump's trusted ally The FBI is assisting local authorities following Graham's death, officials said. FBI DirectorKash Patel said in a statementthat the agency ""is assisting local authorities and has made every necessary resource available. It was not immediately clear how the FBI would be involved, or whether there was any investigation into the death. Also Read:Trump says Lindsey Graham called him hours before his death: 'He was tir","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:55:07 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/lindsey-graham-death-final-moments-photos-show-the-senator-being-wheeled-out-on-a-gurney-as-ems-fought-to-save-him-101783875423612.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Over 200 protesters march to OpenAI, Google DeepMind offices demanding AI regulation and pause in AI race","Over 200 protesters march to OpenAI, Google DeepMind offices demanding AI regulation and pause in AI race","Over 200 protesters march to OpenAI, Google DeepMind offices demanding AI regulation and pause in AI race Over 200 protesters marched to OpenAI and Google DeepMind offices, calling for stricter AI regulation and a pause in developing advanced AI models. Over 200 people joined ‘Stop the A.I. race’—an anti A.I. movement led by activist Michael Trazzi—as they marched towards Open AI and DeepMind offices on San Francisco’s fourth street to demand regulation of AI and halt its progress at its current level, SF Chronicle reported. Protestors carried posters like “stop slop,” “it’s not too late to regulate” and “in a race off a cliff no one wins,” marching from offices of OpenAI to Anthropic andGoogle DeepMind, demanding that their CEOs arrest the further development of the trading models of LLMs, SF chronicle reported. According to the San Francisco Chronicle, the demonstration drew a diverse crowd, including university students, AI industry professionals and longtime San Francisco residents, many of whom said they wanted to raise public awareness about the rapid development of artificial intelligence. Organisers argued that greater public scrutiny could push AI companies to adopt more responsible practices. As protesters marched through downtown San Francisco, onlookers gathered along sidewalks, restaurant patios and apartment balconies, with many stopping to record the procession on their phones. Also read:Apple set to overtake Google as world's second-most valuable company: What's driving the surge? Speaking to the San Francisco Chronicle, Aleesa Carbo, a student at Johns Hopkins University and anAI researcher, said public demonstrations alone may not be enough to drive change, but they can encourage broader civic engagement. S","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:51:01 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/over-200-protesters-march-to-openai-google-deepmind-offices-demanding-ai-regulation-and-pause-in-ai-race-101783875995570.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Trump says Lindsey Graham called him hours before his death: 'He was tired because of long trip',Trump says Lindsey Graham called him hours before his death: 'He was tired because of long trip',"Trump says Lindsey Graham called him hours before his death: 'He was tired because of long trip' Lindsey Graham, South Carolina Republican, died on Sunday after ‘brief and sudden illness’.&nbsp; Lindsey Graham, South Carolina Senator and a close aide of US President Donald Trump, died on Sunday after “brief and sudden illness.” Trump said that the Senator called him on Saturday night after returning from a trip to Ukraine and “sounded a bit tired”. “He sounded a little bit tired, but perfect,” Trump told NBC's ”Meet the Press."" Graham, a staunch pro-Israel and hawkish supporter of Trump's US polices, was last seen in Kyiv, where he went for a visit to meet with Ukrainian President Volodmyr Zelensky.Track live updates for US-Iran news Trump said Graham was “like a member of the family"". He implied that he may have been among the last people to have spoken to Graham before his death. The US President made a similar claim in an interview with CNN's Jake Tapper where he termed Graham's death as ‘devastating’. ""I thought he was fine. He called me last night. He just got back from Ukraine. And he had a great time. He was telling me about the trip. He was working very, very hard, because we know he wanted to make America happy,"" Trump said in the interview. “He was full of vim and vigor. He was tired. He said, ‘I’m tired, because it’s a long trip.’ But other than that, he was fine. And he called me, I guess, moments before, because he called me like 6:30 or something. And the medical people got there a little bit later,” he added. Also read:India declares one-day national mourning for Qatar's Father Amir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani Mourning Graham's death, Trump said ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:15:12 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/donald-trump-says-lindsey-graham-called-him-hours-before-dying-he-was-tired-because-of-long-trip-to-ukraine-101783869477406.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,One index fund that could soar in 2026 and 3 myths every index investor should know,One index fund that could soar in 2026 and 3 myths every index investor should know,"One index fund that could soar in 2026 and 3 myths every index investor should know Learn the biggest index fund myths, why experts are bullish on the S&amp;P 500, and why Vanguard S&amp;P 500 ETF (VOO) could be a top buy in 2026. Index funds are investment funds that copy a market index like the S&P 500 instead of trying to beat it. They collect money from many investors and buy the same stocks that are part of the index they track. Mostindex funds are passively managed, which means they usually have lower fees than actively managed funds. One popular example is the Vanguard S&P 500 ETF (VOO), which tracks the S&P 500 and gives investors exposure to 500 large U.S. companies, according to The Motley Fool. Even though index funds are simple and popular, many people still believe myths about them. Here are the biggest ones. Many people think index funds are totally safe because they simply follow the market. This is false. Index funds avoid the risk of a fund manager making bad investment decisions because they don't rely on active stock picking. However, they still face market risk because if the overall market falls, the value of the index fund also falls. An index fund is only as strong as the index it follows. If the index tracks risky or unusual companies, the fund also becomes riskier, according to The Motley Fool. Experts say investors should still have a diversified portfolio and invest for the long term instead of expecting quick profits. Many investors believe every index fund automatically offers perfect diversification. This is also a myth. Some index funds give much bigger weight to the largest companies because they use market capitalization weighting. This means companies like Nvidia,Apple","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:09:39 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/one-index-fund-that-could-soar-in-2026-and-3-myths-every-investor-should-know-101783871018399.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Jeffrey Newman death: NYC activist against homelessness dies days after husband Jayson Connor fatal cardiac arrest,Jeffrey Newman death: NYC activist against homelessness dies days after husband Jayson Connor fatal cardiac arrest,"Jeffrey Newman death: NYC activist against homelessness dies days after husband Jayson Connor fatal cardiac arrest NYC homeless advocates Jeffrey Newman, 58, and Jayson Connor, 48, died four days apart. Connor suffered cardiac arrest; Newman's cause of death remains unknown. Jeffrey Newman and Jayson Connor, aNew York Citycouple who were popular figures for their work against homelessness in the city, died just days after another, sparking concern among those who followed them on social media. Jeffrey Newman, 58, and Jayson Connor, 48, ran a non-profit for thehomelessin New York City. They have distributed over 180,000 backpacks to homeless individuals on New York City Streets over the last few years. Their work earned them recognition, especially on social media, where thousands of people followed and contributed to their work. The shock for their followers came after Jeffrey Newman announced ina post on Facebookon June 29 saying that Jayson Connor had passed away from a cardiac arrest. The shock of the event doubled down on Newman as he revealed that June 29 was their 22nd anniversary. ""We should be celebrating this milestone together at our favorite restaurant,"" a devastated Newman wrote. ""Instead, I am left dealing with the coroner's office and making decisions I never imagined I would have to face. To say that I am in shock, devastated, and heartbroken would be an understatement. ""Jayson was the love of my life. He was my person. He accepted me for who I am—flaws and all—and loved me unconditionally. We were partners in every possible sense."" Subsequently, Newmanshared a link to a GoFundMeon June 30, which he revealed was launched by a friend, Russ Williamson. As of this writing, the GoFundMe had raised $21,212 of its $28,000 target. Since t","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:08:00 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/jeffrey-newman-cause-of-death-nyc-homelessness-activist-dies-days-after-husband-jayson-connor-fatal-cardiac-arrest-101783872700883.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,FBI 'assisting' in Lindsey Graham death probe? Kash Patel shares major update,FBI 'assisting' in Lindsey Graham death probe? Kash Patel shares major update,"FBI 'assisting' in Lindsey Graham death probe? Kash Patel shares major update Kash Patel opened up about the FBI’s role after US Senator Lindsey Graham’s sudden death as questions continue surrounding the senator’s final days. The FBI has joined local authorities in looking into the sudden death of Senator Lindsey Graham, whose office announced on Sunday that he died after what it described as a “brief and sudden illness.” The 71-year-old South Carolina Republican had returned from a trip to Ukraine just days earlier, where he met President Volodymyr Zelensky and visited military facilities. Reports said a 911 call for cardiac arrest was made from his Washington residence on Saturday evening, but officials have not yet released a confirmed cause of death. FBI Director Kash Patel said the bureau is “assisting local authorities and has made every necessary resource available.” As news of Graham’s death spread, political commentators from across the spectrum questioned the lack of details surrounding what happened. Megan Mobbs, Director of the Center for American Safety & Security at the Independent Women’s Forum, argued that more information is needed before conclusions are reached. “Cardiac arrest tells us how his life ended. It does not tell us why his heart stopped,” Mobbs wrote on X. She added: “Given the threat environment, the identities of America’s adversaries, andSenatorGraham’s prominent role confronting them, the American people deserve certainty.” Mobbs also called for “a complete forensic autopsy, preservation of all relevant biological specimens, comprehensive toxicology and histology, and consultation with federal law enforcement and counterintelligence authorities.” Also Read:Lindsey ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:44:19 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/fbi-assisting-in-lindsey-graham-death-probe-kash-patel-shares-major-update-101783872323145.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Explainer: How OpenAI plans to win the healthcare industry with ChatGPT AI,Explainer: How OpenAI plans to win the healthcare industry with ChatGPT AI,"Explainer: How OpenAI plans to win the healthcare industry with ChatGPT AI OpenAI is expanding into healthcare with ChatGPT, AI tools, hospital partnerships and ChatGPT Health to help patients, doctors and health systems. OpenAI is making healthcare one of its biggest business priorities. OpenAI is now focusing heavily on the healthcare industry because it believes AI can improve healthcare for millions of people. The company says healthcare is now one of its most important business areas, also called a ""vertical."" OpenAI CEO Sam Altman is personally joining meetings with hospital CEOs to convince them to useOpenAI's AI tools. His presence shows how important healthcare has become for the company, according to Forbes. OpenAI believes hospital leaders are more likely to trust the company when Altman explains its vision himself. In January, OpenAI announced that eight major US health systems became customers of its enterprise healthcare tools, according to OpenAI announcement. These include Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and HCA Healthcare. OpenAI has introduced three healthcare-focused products in the last six months. It is rolling out a special version of ChatGPT designed for doctors and clinicians. It is also launching ""ChatGPT Health,"" which lets users securely connect their medical records and wellness apps, according to Forbes. Apps like Apple Health and MyFitnessPal can be connected with ChatGPT Health. The product is currently available only through a waitlist. More than 260 doctors are helping OpenAI improve ChatGPT's medical answers. These doctors review ChatGPT's responses and point out mistakes. They also train the AI to know when it should not answer because it lacks enough information","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:16:20 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/explainer-how-openai-plans-to-win-the-healthcare-industry-with-chatgpt-ai-101783868455391.html,2026-07-13 01:29:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Kalshi users lost nearly $600 million betting against pro traders: Report,Kalshi users lost nearly $600 million betting against pro traders: Report,"Kalshi users lost nearly $600 million betting against pro traders: Report A new report claims Kalshi users lost nearly $600 million betting against professional traders. Here's what the study found and how Kalshi responded. Anew report by the Roosevelt Institute, a New York City-based think tank, claims that regular people using prediction market Kalshi have lost nearly $600 million since the platform started in 2018. According to the report, everyday users have lost about $583.5 million while betting on different real-world events through Kalshi. The study says many regular users do not realize they are often betting against professional traders who use advanced tools and trading strategies. The report argues that this gives professional traders a major advantage over casual users. The study was written by Brad Lipton, who is the Roosevelt Institute's Director of Corporate Power and Financial Regulation. After the report was published, Kalshi strongly rejected the findings and said the report misunderstood how its platform works, as stated by Business Insider. Kalshi said there is no ""house"" on its platform, unlike a casino where the operator wins from customer losses. The company explained that it simply matches buyers and sellers, just like a financial exchange, instead of taking the opposite side of users' bets. Kalshi said the report wrongly suggested that a difference in trading skill means there is a problem with themarket's structure, as noted by Business Insider. The company added that having experienced traders on the platform does not mean the exchange itself is unfair. Also read:Who is the Khosla Family? Meet Vinod Khosla, Neeru Khosla and Neal Khosla behind the Seattle Seahawks deal","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:13:59 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/kalshi-users-lost-nearly-600-million-betting-against-pro-traders-report-101783862369603.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Who could replace Lindsey Graham? How South Carolina will choose the next US senator,Who could replace Lindsey Graham? How South Carolina will choose the next US senator,"Who could replace Lindsey Graham? How South Carolina will choose the next US senator Who could replace Lindsey Graham? Here's how South Carolina will choose a temporary senator, hold a GOP primary, and pick a candidate for November. TheU.S. Senator Lindsey Graham diedat the age of 71, as his office confirmed the news in a statement posted on social media. His office said he died on Saturday evening after a ""brief and sudden illness."" Graham was a Republican senator from South Carolina. He first entered the U.S. Senate in 2002 after serving in the U.S. House of Representatives. He also ran for the Republican presidential nomination in 2016, according to KCRA 3 report. After ending his presidential campaign, Graham became one of President Donald Trump's closest political allies. South Carolina law says Governor Henry McMaster will appoint a temporary replacement toGraham's Senate seat. The temporary senator will serve until January 3 next year. The governor has the power to choose almost anyone who meets the legal requirements. Unlike some other states, South Carolina law does not require the governor to appoint someone from Graham's Republican Party. This means Gov. Henry McMaster has broad freedom in deciding who the temporary senator will be, according to the report by KCRA 3. Graham was running for reelection and had already won the Republican nomination earlier this year. Because he died before the election, Republicans now have to choose a new Senate candidate. A special Republican primary election must be held to pick a new GOP nominee, according to FOX Carolina. The filing period for candidates could begin as early as July 21. Also read:Who is the Khosla Family? Meet Vinod Khosla, Neeru Khosla and ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:19:10 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/who-could-replace-lindsey-graham-how-south-carolina-will-choose-the-next-us-senator-101783859306845.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' hours after Iran 'closes' it: 'Traffic is flowing',US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' hours after Iran 'closes' it: 'Traffic is flowing',"US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' hours after Iran 'closes' it: 'Traffic is flowing' US CENTCOM said their forces “are positioned and prepared to ensure that freedom of navigation remains available…"" Hours after Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps said they were closing the Strait of Hormuz again, the United States said the waterway is “open to all vessels seeking to lawfully transit the waterway.” The US Central Command further said that “traffic is flowing” through the strait, adding that their forces “are positioned and prepared to ensure that freedom of navigation remains available despite unwarranted Iranian aggression, harassment, threats, and arbitrary declarations.” The US CENTCOM asserted that Iran does not control the strait, saying pathways for for free transit remained open.Track live updates on US-Iran war “Iran does not control the international waterway used by commercial vessels to globally transport goods and energy,” CENTCOM said in a post on X. It added that the US forces had facilitated the transit of 800+ ships and over 400 million barrels of crude oil over the last two months. “140+ ships have transited the strait in the last seven days,” it said. Global monitoring body, the Joint Maritime Information Center, had earlier reported that the southern route of the strait near Oman’s coast remained open on Sunday, even after Iran's announcement. US forces struck Iran for a third time in a week earlier on Sunday, following which Tehran retaliated by attacking five Gulf nations and closing the Strait of Hormuz once again “until further notice.” The US CENTCOM said President Donald Trump had ordered fresh strikes targeting Tehran’s ability to attack com","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:02:27 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-says-strait-of-hormuz-open-to-all-hours-after-iran-closes-it-traffic-is-flowing-us-iran-war-west-asia-conflict-101783858763454.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Pak constable killed on duty in terror attack in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,Pak constable killed on duty in terror attack in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,"Pak constable killed on duty in terror attack in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa The constable was sitting inside a police post when a terrorist entered and started firing indiscriminately A police constable was shot dead by an unidentified assailant in a terrorist attack inPakistan'sKhyber Pakhtunkhwaprovince on Sunday, police said. The incident took place in the mountainous district of Buner. Also Read I‘No graveyard in Kashmir without Pakistani terrorists’: Hizbul Mujahideen commander's admission on cam According to preliminary reports, Constable Miskeen Zada was sitting inside apolice postwhen a militant entered the premises and opened indiscriminate fire, killing him on the spot before fleeing the scene. The suspected attacker had reportedly been staying in the area for several days and was believed to have been under the watch of security agencies. Also Read IAsim Munir will now try to control Pakistan's population: Field Marshal put on a high-level committee by Shehbaz Sharif The Counter Terrorism Department (CTD) had conducted raids at various locations to arrest him, but he managed to evade capture. Following the attack, police and other law enforcement agencies cordoned off the area, collected forensic evidence and launched a search operation to trace and apprehend the suspect. Also Read IWhy is foreign investment shrinking in Pakistan? Reason is worsening security climate According to data released by the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Police, 122 police personnel have been killed in the line of duty during the first six months of the current year.","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:04:57 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/pak-constable-killed-on-duty-in-terror-attack-in-khyber-pakhtunkhwa-101783849274345.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Laura Loomer alleges foreign plot in Lindsey Graham's death, seeks probe: ‘Doesn’t feel like coincidence’","Laura Loomer alleges foreign plot in Lindsey Graham's death, seeks probe: ‘Doesn’t feel like coincidence’","Laura Loomer alleges foreign plot in Lindsey Graham's death, seeks probe: ‘Doesn’t feel like coincidence’ Loomer named Iran and Russia, and also pointed out signs against the Republican Senator at late Iranian Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei's funeral. Hours after Lindsey Graham's office released a statement confirming his death, MAGA influencer Laura Loomer questioned the timing and circumstances around it. Loomer claimed Graham's death “doesn't feel like coincidence”, while alleging a foreign plot and calling for a probe. Loomer named Iran and Russia in a series of posts she made regardingGraham's death, wherein she also pointed out signs against the Republican Senator at late Iranian Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei's funeral. The influencer further said Russia had sent a delegation to Khamenei's funeral, and highlighted that Graham had been in Ukraine a day previous to his death speaking about a Russia sanctions bill, which he said the White House supported. Also Read | Lindsey Graham ‘a true patriot, was always working’: Trump's tribute to US senator who died at 71 “5 days ago, the IRGC publicly called for Senator Lindsey Graham to be assassinated. He was traveling abroad to a war zone the last few days to try to end the war between Ukraine and Russia,” Loomer said in a post on X. She further said that Loomer had only been at home for “less than a day” when his staff said he had passed away from a “brief and sudden illness.” “Was he poisoned by a foreign adversary either abroad or upon returning to the US? There should be an investigation into his death. Especially after Iran called for his death less than one week ago. What do his staff mean by a “brief and sudden illness”? Poison?” the influencer questioned in her post. L","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:57:53 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/laura-loomer-alleges-foreign-plot-in-lindsey-graham-death-seeks-probe-doesn-t-feel-like-coincidence-101783847905189.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"How the Patriot missile system works, and why it's so hard to replace","How the Patriot missile system works, and why it's so hard to replace","How the Patriot missile system works, and why it's so hard to replace US President Donald Trump announced a licence for Ukraine to make Patriot systems, capable of shooting down ballistic missiles.&nbsp; US President Donald Trump has agreed to license Ukraine to manufacture its own Patriot missile interceptors, announcing the move at the Nato summit in Ankara in a yet another striking reversal of his earlier scepticism towards Kyiv. “We're going to give a license to you to make Patriots. That's pretty cool. This way, you can't complain that we're not giving ‘em enough,"" Trump told Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky at their meeting on the summit sidelines. “It’s a defensive weapon, which I like better than an offensive weapon,” he added. Trump gave no details on how the licensing arrangement would work or when production might start. Patriot is among a handful of systems worldwide, and the only one of its kind with Ukraine, capable of shooting down ballistic missiles. These missiles travel at high speeds and descend at a steep angle, which makes them hard to intercept. Russia has sharply escalated ballistic missile strikes in recent months, killing dozens of people in Kyiv in the past week alone. Zelensky formally asked Washington for permission to manufacture Patriots under licence in late May. Over the course of the four-year war, Kyiv has managed to counter most Russian drone attacks, but ballistic missiles remain what Zelensky has called Moscow’s “last major advantage”, BBC reported. Ukraine’s air force has said it faces a “serious shortage” of interceptors — a gap starkly illustrated when it failed to shoot down any of the 23 ballistic missiles fired by Russia during","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:50:08 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/how-the-patriot-missile-system-works-and-why-its-so-hard-to-replace-101783853720181.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Iranian newspaper names Trump, Netanyahu, Starmer among leaders on revenge list","Iranian newspaper names Trump, Netanyahu, Starmer among leaders on revenge list","Iranian newspaper names Trump, Netanyahu, Starmer among leaders on revenge list In his first public message since his father Ayatollah Ali Khamenei's funeral earlier this week, Mojtaba Khamenei declared that revenge was unavoidable. An Iranian newspaper known for its hardline and provocative stance has published the names and photographs of several foreign leaders it says should be targeted in retaliation for the killing of Iran's supreme leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, following the outbreak of theUS-Iran war. Ali Khamenei was killed inUS-Israelistrikes on February 28, the opening day of the conflict. His son and successor, Mojtaba Khamenei, has since vowed that those responsible will face retribution. In his first public message since his father's funeral earlier this week, issued on Saturday, Mojtaba Khamenei declared that revenge was unavoidable. ""Vengeance is the will of our nation and must inevitably be carried out,"" he said. ""These criminals, whose names appear on a list, will take to their graves the wish of a peaceful death in their beds."" Later on Saturday, the Hamshahri newspaper, which is published by the authorities in the Iranian capital, shared an online infographic displaying photographs of 13 foreign leaders alongside Mojtaba Khamenei's statement, news agency AFP reported. Although the supreme leader said Iran had prepared a list of individuals to be targeted, he did not identify anyone by name. There was also no indication that the list published by the newspaper had been officially endorsed by the Iranian government. Also Read:'Deeply worrisome': India condemns attack on GFS Galaxy vessel off Oman's coast amid US-Iran war Among those featured in the infographic are US President Donald ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:45:02 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/iranian-newspaper-names-donald-trump-benjamin-netanyahu-keir-starmer-revenge-list-us-iran-war-101783849703890.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Typhoon Bavi weakens, China to receive heavy rains as storm expected to turn","Typhoon Bavi weakens, China to receive heavy rains as storm expected to turn","Typhoon Bavi weakens, China to receive heavy rains as storm expected to turn After making landfall in Zhejiang, Typhoon Bavi is expected to weaken to the level of a severe tropical storm China’s National Meteorological Center saidTyphoon Baviweakened to a severe tropical storm on Sunday morning after making landfall in Zhejiang. The storm is expected to turn northeast in eastern Anhui on July 13 before moving into the northern Yellow Sea and gradually transitioning into an extra-tropical cyclone, the center said. Heavy rainfall is forecast through July 14 across Fujian, Zhejiang, Jiangxi, Anhui, Jiangsu, Shandong and parts of northeasternChina, with forecasters warning of a high risk of rain-related disasters. Some areas of Anhui, Zhejiang and Jiangxi could see extremely heavy downpours, while strong winds may affect shipping, offshore operations and aquaculture along China’s eastern coast. Also Read IChina ravaged by tornadoes, more danger awaits - All about Typhoon Bavi that looms offshore China’s transport ministry raised its emergency response for heavy rainfall to Level II on Sunday and maintained a Level III response for typhoons after the national weather forecaster issued an orange rainstorm alert and a yellow typhoon alert. China’s National Development and Reform Commission has allocated 100 million yuan ($14 million) from the central budget to support emergency recovery efforts in Zhejiang, Xinhua News Agency reported. The funds will be used to repair damaged roads, water conservancy projects, schools and hospitals as authorities seek to restore normal production and daily life. The planning agency also allocated an additional 100 million yuan to su","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:56:45 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/typhoon-bavi-weakens-china-to-receive-heavy-rains-as-storm-expected-to-turn-101783849264021.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,South Korea issues first emergency heatwave warning under new rating system,South Korea issues first emergency heatwave warning under new rating system,"South Korea issues first emergency heatwave warning under new rating system An emergency alert is issued when areas experiencing a heatwave are forecast to hit perceived temperatures of 38C or an actual temperature of 39C for one day. South Korea issued its first-ever emergency heatwave alert on Sunday under a new warning system launched this year, advising people to halt outdoor activities and keep cool. The new warning system was introduced to better deal with a rising number of heatwaves inSouth Korea, which have become longer and more intense, officials said. An emergency alert is issued when areas experiencing a heatwave are forecast to hit perceived temperatures of 38C or an actual temperature of 39C for one day. ""The Korea Meteorological Administration issued an Emergency Heatwave Warning at 10 am today (GMT 0100) for two cities in southern North Gyeongsang Province, Gyeongsan and Pohang,"" said agency chief Lee Mi-seon at a press briefing. ""This marks the first time it has been issued since the system took effect,"" she added. The affected areas saw temperatures reach the emergency criteria over the weekend. ""An emergency heatwave warning does not simply mean the weather is extremely hot,"" Lee said. Also Read:Europe swelters under deadly 'Omega' heatwave, more records broken ""It indicates conditions in which even healthy people face a significantly elevated risk of serious harm, including heat-related illness and death."" People engaged in outdoor activities should stop immediately and move to a cool place, and no one, including children or pets, should be left inside a vehicle, she added. Much of the country, including parts of Seoul, remained under heatwave warnings, which are issued when the percei","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:20:30 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/south-korea-issues-first-emergency-heatwave-warning-under-new-rating-system-101783849204874.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"'No better friend than him': Netanyahu, other Israeli leaders mourn Lindsey Graham's death","'No better friend than him': Netanyahu, other Israeli leaders mourn Lindsey Graham's death","'No better friend than him': Netanyahu, other Israeli leaders mourn Lindsey Graham's death Lindsey Graham was one of Israel's strongest supporters. He consistently backed military aid and would defend the country's continuous wars on Iran and Gaza. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and other senior leaders on Sunday paid tribute to US SenatorLindsey Graham following his death. Graham died on Sunday due to a “sudden illness”. He was 71. Israeli officials described him as one of their closest friends and a steadfast supporter of the US-Israel alliance. On X,Netanyahusaid he and his wife were grieving alongside the American people over the loss of their ""dear friend."" ""Sara and I grieve with the American people over the loss of our dear friend, Senator Lindsey Graham,"" Netanyahu wrote. Recalling a recent meeting with Graham, the Israeli prime minister said, ""Lindsey is a great friend of Israel and a cherished friend of mine. We have no better friend than Lindsey."" Netanyahu praised Graham's longstanding support for Israel, saying, ""Lindsey understood that the security of Israel and America are inseparable. He devoted his life to defending America, strengthening our alliance and standing up for the free world."" ""Israel has lost one of its greatest friends. America has lost a great patriot. I have lost a beloved friend,"" he added. Israeli President Isaac Herzog said he received thenews of Graham's deathwith ""shock and pain,"" calling the senator ""a great friend of Israel and a great American patriot."" ""Senator Graham was a beacon of moral clarity and a true leader of the partnership between the United States and Israel. We will never forget how he stood by the people of Israel in our most difficult moments, and we wil","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:19:34 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/benjamin-netanyahu-others-israeli-leaders-mourn-lindsey-graham-death-says-no-better-friend-than-him-101783847300510.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Indian community in US to open museum on country's culture in Washington DC,Indian community in US to open museum on country's culture in Washington DC,"Indian community in US to open museum on country's culture in Washington DC The India Heritage Centre is currently scouting appropriate locations to open a museum exhibiting India's rich cultural heritage From the Indus Valley Civilisation to a nation on the rise, the India story may soon come alive at a museum inWashington DC-- a first-of-its-kind project aimed at the younger generations of the Indian diaspora. The India Heritage Centre is scouting for a suitable location in the American capital to house thebrick-and-mortar museumthat would use immersive technology, virtual reality, interactive exhibits and multimedia displays to present India's contributions over the years to a global audience. ""The aim is to propagate awareness on India's age-old rich civilisational strength, educating the diaspora, especially younger generations, instilling pride, dispelling ignorance and perhaps sensitising the global multiethnic community,"" Indian-American educationist Amitabh Sharma told PTI. Also Read IWas there a quid pro quo behind case dismissal? US judge seeks Adani's reply by July 15 Sharma has approached theIndian Embassyhere for the use of a building purchased by it in 2013 in the heart of the American capital to set up the museum. This museum is envisioned as a global centre for Indian civilisation, history and heritage, a powerful educational resource for future generations and multiethnic communities, a cultural bridge fostering greater understanding and awareness, and a permanent legacy for the diaspora and supporters worldwide. ""At a time when narratives shape global perception, future generations require authentic institutions that preserve, present, and celebrate India's ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:12:06 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/indian-community-in-us-to-open-museum-on-countrys-culture-in-washington-dc-101783846611027.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Qatar's former emir Sheikh Hamad dies at 74; PM Modi, other world leaders express condolences","Qatar's former emir Sheikh Hamad dies at 74; PM Modi, other world leaders express condolences","Qatar's former emir Sheikh Hamad dies at 74; PM Modi, other world leaders express condolences The news was announced in an official statement by the Amiri Diwan, although no reason for his passing was provided. Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani, formeremir of Qatar, has died at the age of 74, the country's top government body, the Amiri Diwan, announced on Sunday without mentioning the cause of his death. Qatar has declared 4 days of public mourning beginning Monday. Government offices and public institutions will remain closed during this period, while flags across the country will fly at half-mast, Doha-based Al Jazeera reported. Sheikh Hamad, who led Qatar from 1995 until 2013, was seen as a key player in shaping the growth and development of the energy-rich nation. In a statement, the Amiri Diwan said, “With hearts steadfast in faith in God's decree and destiny, the Amiri Diwan mourns the great loss to the nation of the late—may God have mercy on him—His Highness the Father Amir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, who passed away this morning, 27 Muharram 1448 AH, corresponding to 12 July 2026, at the age of nearly 74 years.” Several world leaders, including Prime MinisterNarendra Modi, expressed condolences over the former emir's death. In a post on X,PM Modiwrote, ""We deeply mourn the passing of Father Amir of State of Qatar, HH Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani. A visionary leader who led Qatar to great levels of development and prosperity, we remember him also as a true friend whom I had the honour of meeting during my last visit to Qatar in February 2024,. He added, ""I convey my sincere condolences to the Amir of Qatar, HH Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani and the entire royal","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:53:49 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/former-qatar-emir-sheikh-hamad-passes-away-at-74-pm-modi-and-world-leaders-condole-101783841370682.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Jamey Carney update: Where is Ahmad Alsaqer? Manhunt underway for NY mom's partner after her shocking murder in Ireland,Jamey Carney update: Where is Ahmad Alsaqer? Manhunt underway for NY mom's partner after her shocking murder in Ireland,"Jamey Carney update: Where is Ahmad Alsaqer? Manhunt underway for NY mom's partner after her shocking murder in Ireland A search is underway for Ahmad Alsaqer, an asylum-seeking migrant suspected of beating and suffocating US mom Jamey Carney to death inside her Ireland home. A search is underway for an asylum-seeking migrant suspected of beating and suffocating New York mother Jamey Carney to death inside her Ireland home. Police launched a manhunt for the “significant person of interest.” Ahmad Alsaqer, 28, was reportedly in Turkey by the time police launched a manhunt. He allegedly booked a flight out of Dublin and landed in Istanbul hours before Carney’s daughter, 13, found her mother dead in the bed of their Killarney home on Tuesday, July 7, around 1 pm, Irish Independent reported. Alsaqer applied for asylum after arriving inIrelandfrom the Middle East in 2024, the New York Post reported. He boarded a bus around 3 am for the Irish capital airport after allegedly murdering Carney, his 43-year-old partner, hours earlier. Also Read |Who was Jamey Carney? American woman, 43, found dead in bedroom of Ireland home; murder investigation launched Carney was pronounced dead at her home. The Irish National Police, Gardai, issued an alert, asking the public to help with information about the person of interest seen in the area between 11 pm on Monday, July 6, and 5 am on the following day. According to Extra.ie, police believe Alsaqer will try to travel through the Middle East to get back to Jordan. He reportedly has connections in Turkey,Syriaand Jordan and is fluent in Arabic, French and English. Alsaqer, described by the Gardai as a person of interest in Carney’s murder, is believed to have been one of the last people to see Carney. He spent Sunday ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:48:39 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/jamey-carney-update-where-is-ahmad-alsaqer-manhunt-underway-for-ny-moms-partner-after-her-shocking-murder-in-ireland-101783847292794.html,2026-07-13 01:29:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Why did Lindsey Graham never get married? What late senator revealed, ‘The right girl was smart enough not to…’","Why did Lindsey Graham never get married? What late senator revealed, ‘The right girl was smart enough not to…’","Why did Lindsey Graham never get married? What late senator revealed, ‘The right girl was smart enough not to…’ Late senator Lindsey Graham's self-published memoir, My Story, offered a peek into why he never got married. Details aboutLindsey Graham’spersonal life are being discussed after the senator died at the age of 71. While his office said he died“from a brief and sudden illness,”The Washington Post has now revealed that the senator from South Carolinasuffered chest painat his D.C. home after returning from Ukraine, and then went into cardiac arrest, before dying. Graham's self-published memoir, My Story, offered a peek into why he never got married. In his autobiography, released in 2015, he talked about his brushes with matrimony and opened up about why he never found a wife. “I’ve never married. I guess I attribute that to timing, too,” wrote Graham. “The opportunity never presented itself at the right time, or I never found time to meet the right girl, or the right girl was smart enough not to have time for me.” However, Graham did come close. He had a girlfriend, Debbie, in law school, and then two more during his time in the Air Force in Germany, including a JAG officer named Carol who went on to serve on Colin Powell’s staff, and a Lufthansa flight attendant, Sylvia, according to Politico. Graham wrote that his relationship with Sylvia became “serious quickly” and he considered proposing to her. However, he never did. She eventually returned to Vienna to be with her family and he “was a South Carolina boy who needed to go home.” “I’ve been close once early on, [as I was] taking care of my sister,” Graham said in the past about not getting married, per Politico. “It’s something I r","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:55:52 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/why-did-lindsey-graham-never-get-married-what-late-senator-revealed-the-right-girl-was-smart-enough-not-to-101783844484420.html,2026-07-13 01:29:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Europe is hot, crowded and crazy expensive. Here’s how to enjoy it anyway.","Europe is hot, crowded and crazy expensive. Here’s how to enjoy it anyway.","Europe is hot, crowded and crazy expensive. Here’s how to enjoy it anyway. Americans are finding ways to navigate the new reality of vacationing in Europe. Experts share their best tips to make the most out of a trip across the pond. The sun was beating down on the Greek island of Crete last month,and the tourists were out in full force: dining on gyros along the harbor, buying trinkets in souvenir shops, zipping around the coastline on boats. “We are hooked on traveling now,” said Lisa Mallo, 54, as she waited with her husband, Wesley, for a midday boat tour departing from the 14th-century harbor in the city of Chania. The couple from Florida was nearing the end of a 10-day island-hop around Greece, one of their first without kids—and they had plenty of company from their countrymen. Americans are still flocking to Europe in droves this summer, despiterecord-breaking heat, higher airfare prices and long immigration lines due to the chaotic rollout of a new screening system in some European countries. Thedollar has also weakenedover the past year and a half, down nearly 10% against the euro since the start of 2025, sapping the purchasing power of travelers. Nearly 11 million U.S. citizens have flown to Europe between January and June, up 2.2% compared to the same period last year, according to International Trade Administration data. Find yourself in Europe among the crowd? Read on for tips from frequent travelers and travel advisers on how to enjoy its destinations without facing endless lines or scary prices. The best way to avoid crowds has always been to go where they’re not. Cecile Blot, owner of travel agency Boundless Travels, is pushing clients to consider places like Slovenia, for its mountain vi","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:47:48 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/europe-is-hot-crowded-and-crazy-expensive-here-s-how-to-enjoy-it-anyway-101783844199585.html,2026-07-13 01:29:43
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"India-UK FTA: Zero tariffs open UK market, but can Indian MSMEs beat China, Bangladesh and Vietnam?","India-UK FTA: Zero tariffs open UK market, but can Indian MSMEs beat China, Bangladesh and Vietnam?","India-UK FTA: Zero tariffs open UK market, but can Indian MSMEs beat China, Bangladesh and Vietnam? India-UK FTA comes into effect on July 15, offering zero-duty access to Indian exporters. But MSMEs face challenges from China, Bangladesh and Vietnam as competitiveness, compliance and logistics become key India’s trade ambitions in the UK are set to enter a new phase on July 15, when the India-UK Comprehensive Economic and Trade Agreement (CETA) comes into effect. The agreement promises near-zero duty access for Indian exporters, with nearly 99 per cent of India’s exports to Britain set to receive preferential market access. From textiles and leather to gems and jewellery, food processing and engineering goods, several sectors are expected to gain from the removal of tariff barriers. But for India’s micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs), the biggest challenge begins after the tariff cuts. The question is no longer whether Indian companies can enter the UK market. The question is whether they can compete against established manufacturing hubs such as China, Bangladesh and Vietnam, which already have strong supply chains and deep relationships with British buyers. Trade experts say the FTA provides Indian exporters with an opportunity, but tariff reductions alone will not automatically lead to a surge in orders. The UK represents a major opportunity for Indian businesses. Britain imported goods worth nearly $929 billion globally in 2025, but India’s share remained limited. India supplied goods worth around $15 billion to the UK market, accounting for just about 1.6 per cent of Britain’s merchandise imports. The low market share highlights the potential for growth, but analysts caution that it should not be mistaken for guaranteed export gains. Indian companies will need to","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:55:53 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/business/india-uk-fta-zero-tariffs-uk-market-indian-msmes-china-bangladesh-vietnam-14030886.html,2026-07-13 01:29:43
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Indian-origin Nasa astronaut Anil Menon set for first space mission aboard Soyuz spacecraft,Indian-origin Nasa astronaut Anil Menon set for first space mission aboard Soyuz spacecraft,"Indian-origin Nasa astronaut Anil Menon set for first space mission aboard Soyuz spacecraft Anil Menon, a doctor, Space Force colonel and Nasa astronaut, is set to begin his first mission in orbit as part of Expeditions 74 and 75 aboard the International Space Station Indian-origin Nasa astronaut Anil Menon is set to embark on his first journey into space on Tuesday, launching aboard the Nasa-Roscosmos Soyuz MS-29 spacecraft. The spacecraft is scheduled to lift off at 10:47 am EDT (2:47 pm UTC) from the historic Baikonur Cosmodrome in Kazakhstan, carrying Menon and two Russian cosmonauts on an eight-month research mission aboard the Nasa International Space Station (ISS). Menon will serve as a flight engineer during Nasa Expeditions 74 and 75, working alongside experienced Russian cosmonauts Pyotr Dubrov and Anna Kikina. The Soyuz spacecraft is expected to complete a quick two-orbit rendezvous before autonomously docking with the Nasa ISS’s Prichal module less than three hours after launch. Born in Minneapolis, Minnesota, Menon’s journey to becoming a Nasa astronaut has brought together medicine, engineering, military service and space exploration. The 49-year-old emergency medicine physician is also a colonel in the US Space Force. He earned a bachelor’s degree in neurobiology from Harvard University, a master’s degree in mechanical engineering from Stanford University, and a Doctor of Medicine degree from Stanford Medical School. The son of Ukrainian and Indian immigrants, Menon built a career around working in some of the most challenging environments before joining Nasa’s astronaut programme. Before wearing a Nasa spacesuit, Menon worked in several demanding roles. As a military flight surgeon, he served with the US Air Force and was d","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:56:12 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/indian-origin-nasa-astronaut-anil-menon-set-for-first-space-mission-aboard-soyuz-spacecraft-14030887.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Vietnam boat tragedy: Survivors allege crew negligence, delayed rescue worsened death toll","Vietnam boat tragedy: Survivors allege crew negligence, delayed rescue worsened death toll","Vietnam boat tragedy: Survivors allege crew negligence, delayed rescue worsened death toll Survivors of the Vietnam speedboat disaster that killed 15 Indian tourists alleged crew negligence and delays in rescue and medical treatment contributed to the high death toll Survivors of the speedboat accident near Hon May Rut Ngoai Island in Vietnam, which claimed the lives of 15 Indian tourists, have alleged that crew negligence, delayed rescue efforts and slow emergency medical care worsened the tragedy. Vietnamese police have detained the captain of a speedboat. 57-year-old Nguyen Hong Hai is under investigation for alleged violations of waterway transport safety regulations, according to the state media. The accident occurred less than 500 metres off the island on Saturday afternoon as the closed speedboat, carrying 32 Indian tourists and four crew members, was returning from Phu Quoc Island. The victims included 10 tourists from Tamil Nadu, three from Andhra Pradesh and two from Kerala, while 17 others were injured. Passengers who survived said the vessel overturned within seconds after being struck by rough seas and strong winds. They also claimed that quicker rescue operations and timely medical treatment could have saved more lives. The 15 victims were part of a company-sponsored trip organised by Lava International, the Indian smartphone and consumer electronics manufacturer said. The tour included the company’s employees, distributors and retail partners. Among those on the trip was Ashish Kumar, a 48-year-old Lava distributor from Guntur, who said the group had divided into three batches to travel between islands. He witnessed the accident from the shore. “We screamed, ‘Help! Help!’,” he toldThe Associated Press, adding that the boat ","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:33:16 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/vietnam-boat-tragedy-survivors-allege-crew-negligence-delayed-rescue-worsened-death-toll-14030884.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Lindsey Graham died of aortic dissection. Why Indians should not ignore this heart condition,Lindsey Graham died of aortic dissection. Why Indians should not ignore this heart condition,"Lindsey Graham died of aortic dissection. Why Indians should not ignore this heart condition A tear in the body’s largest artery claimed Lindsey Graham’s life. Experts warn that South Asians are more vulnerable to the same vascular risks The sudden death of US Senator Lindsey Graham at the age of 71 has drawn attention to a little-known but deadly cardiovascular condition — aortic dissection. Graham was initially reported to have died after a “brief and sudden illness”. However, a preliminary medical examiner’s report later revealed that the cause of death was aortic dissection triggered by arteriosclerotic cardiovascular disease (atherosclerosis). The condition occurs when a tear develops in the inner layer of the aorta, the body’s largest artery. Blood then forces its way through the tear, separating the layers of the artery wall. In severe cases, this can lead to a life-threatening rupture. While Graham’s death has brought the condition into focus in the US, doctors have long warned that people of South Asian origin, including Indians, face a higher and earlier risk of cardiovascular disease. For years, researchers have studied what is known as the South Asian cardiovascular paradox. Despite having, on average, lower rates of smoking and lower body mass indexes (BMIs) compared to many Western populations, South Asians experience significantly higher rates of heart disease. Studies have shown that Indians are more likely to develop cardiovascular problems at a younger age — often five to 10 years earlier than other ethnic groups. Conditions that typically appear in Western patients in their 70s can emerge among South Asians in their 40s and 50s. Experts say genetics plays a role, particularly a higher tende","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:26:16 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/lindsey-graham-died-of-aortic-dissection-why-indians-should-not-ignore-this-heart-condition-14030883.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Globe at a glance: From Cyclospora outbreak in US to Bangkok bar fire,Globe at a glance: From Cyclospora outbreak in US to Bangkok bar fire,"Globe at a glance: From Cyclospora outbreak in US to Bangkok bar fire Your window to world news: Fresh US strikes on Iran, Bangkok's deadly pub fire, Cyclospora spreads across the US, McConnell delays Senate return, a Paris wildfire, Chile festival tragedy and the latest on Lindsey Graham's death — here's your roundup for the day US launches fresh strikes on Iran:The US Central Command said it launched another round of strikes against Iran at 5 pm ET, targeting its ability to threaten civilian mariners and commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz. The military said the action was ordered by the US President to hold Iranian forces accountable. Bangkok pub fire:At least 27 people were killed and 63 others injured after a massive fire ripped through a pub in Bangkok’s Chatuchak district shortly before midnight. Witnesses said smoke was first seen coming from a circuit breaker near the stage before a power outage and explosion. Authorities are investigating the exact cause of the blaze, while many victims were found trapped near the venue’s restrooms. Lindsey Graham died of aortic rupture:A preliminary medical examiner’s report found that US Senator Lindsey Graham died from an aortic rupture (aortic dissection) caused by underlying arteriosclerotic cardiovascular disease, dispelling online speculation about poisoning or assassination. Authorities said further toxicology and microscopic tests are pending before a final cause of death is issued. McConnell delays Senate return:Former Senate Republican leader Mitch McConnell said he will not return to the US Senate yet as he continues recovering from a June fall that left him briefly unconscious and led to pneumonia. The 84-year-old senator is undergoing rehabilitation and physical therapy, saying doctors have advised him to focus on regaining strength bef","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 06:14:15 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/globe-at-a-glance-from-cyclospora-outbreak-in-us-to-bangkok-bar-fire-14030876.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Massive wildfire near Paris forces evacuations, disrupts travel amid France heatwave","Massive wildfire near Paris forces evacuations, disrupts travel amid France heatwave","Massive wildfire near Paris forces evacuations, disrupts travel amid France heatwave A fast-moving wildfire in the Fontainebleau forest south of Paris has triggered evacuations and major travel disruptions as France battles its third heatwave of the year A large wildfire broke out in the Fontainebleau forest, around 60 kilometres (40 miles) south-east of Paris, on Sunday, prompting authorities to deploy firefighting aircraft from southern France as the blaze spread rapidly during a busy summer travel weekend. Officials described the fire as “very virulent” and of “exceptional scale” after it tore through 800 hectares by early Monday, with flames continuing to advance. The wildfire also forced the partial closure of the A6 motorway, France’s main north-south transport route. Aerial firefighting operations were suspended after nightfall, leaving ground crews to continue battling the flames. Around 15 homes were evacuated in the nearby village of Vaudoue, while firefighters worked to protect several neighbouring communities from the advancing fire. Olivier Compta, who is leading the firefighting operation, said other villages would already have been evacuated had firefighting aircraft not been deployed. Nearly 400 firefighters were involved in the response as the blaze erupted just before France’s July 14 national holiday and the first major weekend of the summer holiday travel season. The wildfire disrupted road traffic across the region and also affected the high-speed railway linking Paris with southeastern France. Eric Brocardi, from France’s national federation of firemen, said it was the first time water bomber aircraft had been dispatched from the country’s typically hotter and drier south to tackle a wildfire in the Pari","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:47:01 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/massive-wildfire-near-paris-forces-evacuations-disrupts-travel-amid-france-heatwave-14030880.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Bangkok pub fire kills at least 27; authorities investigate circuit breaker, blocked exits","Bangkok pub fire kills at least 27; authorities investigate circuit breaker, blocked exits","Bangkok pub fire kills at least 27; authorities investigate circuit breaker, blocked exits At least 27 people were killed and 63 injured after a massive fire ripped through a packed live music bar in Bangkok. Investigators are probing reports of an electrical fault and possible blocked fire exits that may have trapped victims At least 27 people were killed and 63 injured after a massive blaze engulfed a crowded bar and live music venue in Bangkok on Sunday night. The fire erupted at the Rong Beer Na Lat Phrao bar and restaurant on the outskirts of the Thai capital. According to Bangkok Governor Chadchart Sittipunt, 22 of the injured remain in critical condition, while authorities have launched an investigation into the cause of the disaster. Emergency responders arrived within minutes, but officials said the fire had already engulfed the venue, making rescue operations extremely difficult. AnAFPjournalist at the scene saw multiple body bags outside the bar as firefighters and rescue workers continued search operations into the early hours of Monday. Witnesses described scenes of chaos as flames burst through the entrance of the venue and smoke rapidly filled the building. Motorbike taxi driver Surin Jaiharn said he rushed to help patrons fleeing the fire, using clothing to extinguish flames on victims whose skin had been badly burned. “I saw many deaths and I do not know the fate of the people I helped,” he toldAFP. Laotian tourist Kan Kutirat, who was inside the venue at the time, said he noticed smoke rising near the stage before hearing screams from inside. “I never experienced anything like this before. The images are still stuck in my mind,” he toldAFP, adding that he managed to carry one woman out of the burning building. Videos circulating on social media showed terrified patrons, some with","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:49:36 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/bangkok-pub-fire-kills-at-least-27-authorities-investigate-circuit-breaker-blocked-exits-14030878.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Iran says 'barbaric' US attacks have 'rendered futile' regional peace efforts,Iran says 'barbaric' US attacks have 'rendered futile' regional peace efforts,"Iran says 'barbaric' US attacks have 'rendered futile' regional peace efforts Iran has condemned the latest US strikes, accusing Washington of undermining months of diplomatic efforts and destabilising the Strait of Hormuz Iran on Sunday accused the United States of derailing months of diplomatic efforts after Washington launched a new round of military strikes, with Tehran saying the attacks had “rendered futile” attempts to ease regional tensions. The condemnation came shortly after theUS military confirmed it had carried out another wave of strikeson Iranian targets. US Central Command (Centcom) said the operation was intended to “continue degrading” Iran’s ability to attack commercial ships transiting the Strait of Hormuz. In a statement, Iran’s foreign ministry described the latest attacks as “barbaric” and accused Washington of breaching international law. “These barbaric attacks are not only a gross violation of the fundamental principles of the United Nations Charter…but also a serious threat to international peace and security,” the ministry said. It added that the strikes had “rendered futile all efforts of the past few months to reduce tension and establish peace in the West Asian region”. Iran also blamed the United States for disrupting maritime security in the Strait of Hormuz. “The US regime has also caused the return of insecurity in the Strait of Hormuz and disruption of international commercial shipping by openly interfering in the process of Iran implementing the necessary arrangements in the Strait of Hormuz,” the statement said. US Central Command said the latest military operation began at 2100 GMT on Sunday, adding in a post on X that President Donald Trump “has directed ","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:24:37 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-says-barbaric-us-attacks-have-rendered-futile-regional-peace-efforts-14030875.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Israeli strikes kill at least six in Gaza, including child, as ceasefire talks continue","Israeli strikes kill at least six in Gaza, including child, as ceasefire talks continue","Israeli strikes kill at least six in Gaza, including child, as ceasefire talks continue The attacks came as mediators continued efforts to keep the US-brokered ceasefire between Israel and Hamas on track despite ongoing violence. At least six Palestinians, including a nine-year-old girl, were killed in Israeli strikes across the Gaza Strip on Sunday, according to Palestinian health officials, even as mediators continued negotiations aimed at preserving the US-brokered ceasefire. The latest violence comes amid ongoing efforts to advance the next phase of the truce between Israel and Hamas. Palestinian medics said nine-year-old Tala Abu Matar was killed after Israeli gunfire struck a tent encampment on the eastern edge of the Al-Bureij refugee camp in central Gaza. The Israeli military said it was not aware of the reported incident. In Gaza City, an Israeli airstrike on a metal foundry in the Sabra neighbourhood killed four people. Witnesses said the site was hit by three missiles. The Israeli military said the strike in Gaza City targeted Hamas militants operating inside a weapons production facility, accusing the group of violating the ceasefire by using the site for military purposes. The military also said its forces had killed at least two Hamas fighters in northern Gaza since Thursday, alleging they were planning attacks on Israeli troops. Later on Sunday, another Israeli strike hit a tent encampment in the Mawasi area of Khan Younis in southern Gaza, killing at least one person and injuring several others, including children, according to medics. The attacks took place as Hamas officials were in Cairo for fresh talks on implementing the second phase of the ceasefire agreement brokered by the Unit","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:48:34 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israeli-strikes-kill-at-least-six-in-gaza-including-child-as-ceasefire-talks-continue-14030872.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,China's own geologists warn of active fault under Brahmaputra mega dam in Tibet,China's own geologists warn of active fault under Brahmaputra mega dam in Tibet,"China's own geologists warn of active fault under Brahmaputra mega dam in Tibet A Chinese geological study has identified an active fault beneath the Brahmaputra hydropower project in Tibet, warning it could threaten the dam's structural stability despite Beijing's repeated assurances on safety and disaster prevention. A study by Chinese geologists has raised fresh concerns over the safety of China’s massive hydropower project on the Brahmaputra River, identifying an active fault line beneath the construction site in Tibet that could undermine the stability of the dam and related infrastructure. The findings contrast with Beijing’s longstanding assertions that the project has been designed to the highest safety standards and would help reduce disaster risks in the region. The multi-billion-dollar project, located close to the Indian border in Arunachal Pradesh, is being built on the Yarlung Tsangpo—China’s name for the Brahmaputra—where the river bends sharply before entering India and later flowing into Bangladesh. According to a report by the South China Morning Post, the researchers found that the Paizhen Fault in eastern Tibet remains geologically active and poses a significant risk to the structural integrity of the hydropower station and associated infrastructure. The findings were published last month in the Chinese-language journal Sedimentary Geology and Tethyan Geology under the supervision of the state-owned China Geological Survey. The researchers warned that the fault, which has remained active since the Pleistocene epoch, could affect dams, reservoirs, roads, bridges and tunnels in the vicinity. Continuous tectonic activity has fractured surrounding rock formations, weakening the foundations on which major engineering structures would rest. The study noted that the Paizhen reg","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:36:07 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/chinas-own-study-warns-of-active-fault-beneath-brahmaputra-dam-site-in-tibet-ws-e-14030861.html,2026-07-13 01:29:44
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,'Sent to hell': Iran state TV clip celebrating Lindsey Graham's death goes viral,'Sent to hell': Iran state TV clip celebrating Lindsey Graham's death goes viral,"'Sent to hell': Iran state TV clip celebrating Lindsey Graham's death goes viral The clip surfaced after Graham, a close ally of US President Donald Trump and a vocal critic of Iran, died following what his office described as a ""brief and sudden illness."" A video of an Iranian state television anchor appearing to celebrate the death of US Senator Lindsey Graham has gone viral on social media, drawing widespread attention amid heightened tensions between Tehran and Washington. Graham, a senior Republican senator and one of US President Donald Trump’s closest political allies, died on Saturday following what his office described as a “brief and sudden illness.” In the widely shared clip, the anchor describes Graham as a “warmongering” and “anti-Iranian” politician before congratulating the Iranian people over his death. Iranian state TV aired a message on Sunday congratulating viewers after the death of US Senator Lindsey Graham, describing him as “warmongering.”pic.twitter.com/PImewLxwoy “I congratulate the great nation of Iran on Lindsey Graham, the warmongering, anti-Iranian US senator, being sent to hell,” the anchor says in the video. The clip was shared on X by Iran International. However, Firstpost could not independently verify the authenticity of the footage. Graham was among the strongest advocates of a hardline US policy toward Iran and consistently backed close strategic ties between the United States and Israel. A longtime ally of President Trump, the South Carolina senator supported military action against Iran and was a prominent supporter of Trump’s judicial appointments, immigration agenda and foreign policy initiatives. Just a day before his death, Graham had announced an agreement with the Trump administration","Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:25:26 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/sent-to-hell-iran-state-tv-clip-celebrating-lindsey-grahams-death-goes-viral-14030869.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US launches fresh strikes on Iranian missile systems around Strait of Hormuz,US launches fresh strikes on Iranian missile systems around Strait of Hormuz,"US launches fresh strikes on Iranian missile systems around Strait of Hormuz The United States launched fresh strikes on Iranian military assets around the Strait of Hormuz after a container ship attack, as Tehran retaliated against Gulf states and the UN appealed for an immediate return to diplomacy. The United States launched a fresh round of military strikes on Iranian missile and air defence systems around the Strait of Hormuz on Sunday after Tehran attacked a container ship in the strategic waterway, further escalating tensions that have pushed the fragile US-Iran interim peace framework to the brink. Iran responded by targeting several Gulf nations, while the United Nations called for an immediate halt to hostilities and a return to negotiations. According to Axios, citing a senior US official, American forces struck Iranian missile batteries, air defence systems and small speed boats operated by the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) at multiple locations around the Strait of Hormuz. The official said the operation was intended to weaken Iran’s capability to launch further attacks on commercial shipping. Iranian state media reported that between 10 and 11 projectiles struck military targets on Qeshm Island, located in the Strait of Hormuz, on Sunday afternoon. Hossein Amir Teymouri, governor of Qeshm township, told the IRNA news agency that all the targets were military installations and that no casualties had been reported. Explosions were also heard in Bandar Abbas, a key Iranian port city overlooking the Gulf, and Hajiabad further inland, according to IRNA. The latest exchange followed a US strike launched in retaliation for an Iranian attack on a container ship transiting the Strait of Hormuz. The vessel caught fire during the assault, leaving one crew mem","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:35:36 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-strikes-iranian-missile-systems-around-strait-of-hormuz-report-14030866.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"'He was tired, but fine': Trump recalls final call with Lindsey Graham hours before his death","'He was tired, but fine': Trump recalls final call with Lindsey Graham hours before his death","'He was tired, but fine': Trump recalls final call with Lindsey Graham hours before his death Trump recalled their final phone conversation, saying Graham sounded tired after returning from Ukraine but otherwise appeared to be ""fine."" US President Donald Trump said on Sunday that he may have been among the last people to speak with Republican Senator Lindsey Graham before the longtime South Carolina lawmaker died unexpectedly at the age of 71. Graham’s office announced his death earlier in the day, prompting tributes from political leaders in the United States and abroad. Speaking to NBC’s Meet the Press, Trump said Graham had called him on Saturday evening to discuss the proposed SAVE America Act, despite telling him he was tired after returning from a trip to Ukraine. “He actually said he was tired, but he wanted to pass the SAVE America Act, and I said, ‘Well, we’re going to get it done, Lindsey. We’re going to get it done. I’ll see you soon,’” Trump said, adding that the two had expected to meet on Sunday. The president said Graham appeared well during the call apart from fatigue. “He was tired because it was a long trip. But other than that, he was fine,” Trump said. “I guess he called me just moments before. What a terrible loss it is.” Trump added that he believed Graham’s death came quickly. “Other than being tired, he was fine. It was a quick end, and maybe that’s not the worst way to go,” he said. In separate remarks on CNN’s State of the Union, Trump said Graham had also spoken about his recent visit to Ukraine, describing it as “a great trip.” The president remembered Graham as one of his closest political allies. “He was like a member of the family to me,” Trump said. He also praised Graham’s ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 23:32:24 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/he-was-tired-but-fine-trump-recalls-final-call-with-lindsey-graham-hours-before-his-death-14030862.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Lindsey Graham's death sets stage for South Carolina Senate seat battle as Trump hints at a favorite,Lindsey Graham's death sets stage for South Carolina Senate seat battle as Trump hints at a favorite,"Lindsey Graham's death sets stage for South Carolina Senate seat battle as Trump hints at a favorite The sudden passing of Senator Lindsey Graham has triggered an immediate political scramble in South Carolina, as Republican factions eye his seat and President Donald Trump signals a preferred successor. The death of veteran Republican Senator Lindsey Graham has not only left a major void in US politics but also set in motion a closely watched succession battle in South Carolina, where Republicans are already positioning themselves for one of the party’s most consequential Senate races. Graham, 71, died on Saturday after what his office described as a ""brief and sudden illness.""A close ally of President Donald Trump and one of the Senate’s most influential voices on foreign policy, Graham’s death ends a political career spanning more than three decades while opening a contest that could reshape the Republican Party’s power dynamics in the Senate. Under South Carolina law, Governor Henry McMaster will appoint an interim senator to fill the vacancy. The appointment, however, is only temporary. State law requires a special election process in which political parties nominate candidates before voters elect a senator to serve a fresh six-year term beginning in January. Even before the succession process formally begins, speculation has intensified over who could emerge as the Republican nominee. President Trump, who shared a close relationship with Graham during his second term, has indicated he already has a preferred candidate, making his endorsement a potentially decisive factor in the contest. Several Republican leaders are reportedly being discussed as possible contenders, including Representatives Nancy Mace and Russell Fry. Whoever ultimately secures the nomination will inh","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:44:09 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/lindsey-grahams-death-sets-stage-for-south-carolina-senate-seat-battle-as-trump-hints-at-a-favorite-14030859.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Apple plans new Apple pencils, expands iPhone tap to pay in stores: Report","Apple plans new Apple pencils, expands iPhone tap to pay in stores: Report","Apple plans new Apple pencils, expands iPhone tap to pay in stores: Report Apple is reportedly planning new Apple Pencils with replaceable batteries while expanding iPhone-based Tap to Pay across its retail stores. Apart from the expected launch of the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Ultra in September, Apple is reportedly planning to unveil several new products during the first half of next year. According to the latest edition of Bloomberg’s Power On newsletter by Mark Gurman, the company is preparing to launch a new lineup of Apple Pencil styluses alongside its next-generation iPad Pro models. Gurman also reports that a redesigned entry-level MacBook Pro and refreshed iPad Pro models are expected to debut around spring next year. Accompanying the new iPads, Apple is also said to be introducing updated Apple Pencil styluses. According to the report, Apple is developing two new Pencil variants. One, codenamed B582, is expected to be an updated version of the entry-level Apple Pencil, while the other, B632, will reportedly be a refreshed version of the Apple Pencil Pro, which was first introduced alongside the M4 iPad Pro in 2024. Gurman adds that Apple is redesigning the styluses as part of its broader efforts to comply with the European Union’s repairability requirements. The new Apple Pencils are expected to feature more easily replaceable batteries—a significant improvement over the current-generation models, which are glued together and notoriously difficult to repair. Apple has also been gradually replacing its customised Isaac payment terminals in retail stores with standard iPhones that support the company’s Tap to Pay feature. Customers visiting Apple Stores may have already noticed e","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:33:45 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/apple-plans-new-apple-pencils-expands-iphone-tap-to-pay-in-stores-report-14030857.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,India declares 1-day national mourning after death of Qatar's Father Amir Sheikh Hamad,India declares 1-day national mourning after death of Qatar's Father Amir Sheikh Hamad,"India declares 1-day national mourning after death of Qatar's Father Amir Sheikh Hamad MEA said the national flag would be flown at half-mast across India on all buildings where it is regularly displayed, while there would be no official entertainment during the day of mourning. The Government of India has declared one day of national mourning on July 13 following the death of Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani, the Father Amir of Qatar and the country’s former emir. The Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) said the national flag would be flown at half-mast across India on all buildings where it is regularly displayed, while there would be no official entertainment during the day of mourning. In a statement, the MEA said the decision was taken as a mark of respect for Sheikh Hamad, who passed away on Sunday. “Government of India has declared one-day national mourning tomorrow, 13 July 2026, as a mark of respect for His Highness Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani, Father Amir of the State of Qatar, who passed away today. The National Flag will be flown at half-mast on the day of mourning throughout India on all buildings where the National Flag is flown regularly and there will be no official entertainment on the day,” the ministry said. Prime Minister Narendra Modi expressed condolences over Sheikh Hamad’s death, describing him as a visionary leader who transformed Qatar and strengthened ties with India. “We feel profound sadness at the death of the Father Amir of the State of Qatar, His Highness Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al-Thani. He was a visionary leader who guided Qatar to great levels of development and prosperity. We also remember him as a true friend whom I had the honour of meeting during my last visit to Qatar in February 2024,” Modi said. The ME","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:17:22 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/india-declares-1-day-national-mourning-after-death-of-qatars-father-amir-sheikh-hamad-14030856.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,'India critical to Indo-Pacific balance': Australia's Penny Wong backs New Delhi's strategic role amid China concerns,'India critical to Indo-Pacific balance': Australia's Penny Wong backs New Delhi's strategic role amid China concerns,"'India critical to Indo-Pacific balance': Australia's Penny Wong backs New Delhi's strategic role amid China concerns Australian Foreign Minister Penny Wong has described India as indispensable to the Indo-Pacific's strategic balance, reinforcing Canberra's commitment to closer ties with New Delhi as regional security concerns over China's military activities deepen. Australia’s Foreign Minister Penny Wong has described India as a cornerstone of the Indo-Pacific’s strategic balance, underscoring the growing importance Canberra places on its relationship with New Delhi amid rising regional security challenges linked to China’s expanding military activities. Asked in a television interview how significant Prime Minister Narendra Modi and India would be in addressing regional security concerns, especially in light of India’s disputed border with China and Beijing’s recent missile test in the Pacific, Australian Foreign Minister Penny Wong said, “India is critical to the strategic balance in our region. India is one of the foremost relationships for us.” Her remarks come at a time when Australia and India are expanding cooperation across defence, maritime security, critical minerals, trade and technology as both countries seek to promote a free, open and rules-based Indo-Pacific. Journalist: India 🇮🇳 shares a border with 🇨🇳China which has fired missiles into Australia's backyard. How important are PM Modi & India in responding to this?🇦🇺Australia FM: India🇮🇳 is critical to our region's strategic balance & one of our most important partnerspic.twitter.com/SfeTtC68ep Wong’s comments follow China’s recent missile launch into the Pacific Ocean, a test that highlighted Beijing’s advancing strategic capabilities and prompted renewed attention to the evolving security environment in the Indo-Pacific. Defence analysts have viewed the launch as a demo","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:05:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/india-critical-to-indo-pacific-balance-australias-penny-wong-backs-new-delhis-strategic-role-amid-china-concerns-14030852.html,2026-07-13 01:29:45
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Israel's Knesset election to be held on October 27 as Netanyahu completes full term,Israel's Knesset election to be held on October 27 as Netanyahu completes full term,"Israel's Knesset election to be held on October 27 as Netanyahu completes full term The decision puts Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on track to complete a full term in office despite mounting criticism over his government's handling of national security. Israel’s governing coalition, led by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, announced on Sunday that the country’s next general election will be held on October 27, 2026, the latest date permitted under Israeli law. According to Haaretz, the announcement means Netanyahu’s current government is on course to complete a full term if the election is held as scheduled. The decision ends months of speculation over the timing of Israel’s next national vote. By holding the election on the final legally permitted date, the coalition will have served its full mandate. Netanyahu, Israel’s longest-serving prime minister, has remained in office for nearly two decades across multiple terms. The election announcement comes as Netanyahu continues to face public criticism over his government’s handling of national security, particularly the events leading up to Hamas’s October 7, 2023 attack on southern Israel. This is a developing story. First Published:July 12, 2026, 20:36 IST First Published:July 12, 2026, 20:36 IST US, Japan, Philippines & 11 nations marked the 2016 SCS ruling anniversary, reaffirming China's SCS claims are baseless. They call the ruling ""final & binding,"" China rejects it. Nations oppose unilateral actions & back freedom of navigation.","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:36:16 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israels-knesset-election-to-be-held-on-october-27-as-netanyahu-completes-full-term-14030851.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Ukraine PM Yulia Svyrydenko resigns as Zelenskyy unveils major government reshuffle,Ukraine PM Yulia Svyrydenko resigns as Zelenskyy unveils major government reshuffle,"Ukraine PM Yulia Svyrydenko resigns as Zelenskyy unveils major government reshuffle Svyrydenko, Ukraine’s former economy minister, was named prime minister in July 2025 at the age of 39 after playing a lead role in securing a mineral agreement between Ukraine and the U.S., seen as an important way of tying US interests to Ukraine’s security. Ukrainian Prime Minister Yulia Svyrydenko resigned on Sunday after President Volodymyr Zelenskyy unveiled a fresh restructuring of his government, describing it as part of a new political strategy. In a statement posted on social media, Svyrydenko reflected on her tenure, saying she was “proud to have had the honor of leading the government during one of the most difficult periods in Ukraine’s modern history.” She added that she had discussed her future role with Zelenskyy but did not reveal further details. “I remain ready to serve the Ukrainian state and carry out every task aimed at strengthening Ukraine’s position, defending our national interests and bringing a just peace closer,” she said. Svyrydenko, who previously served as economy minister, became Ukraine’s prime minister in July 2025 at the age of 39. Her appointment followed her key role in negotiating a minerals agreement with the United States, which was widely viewed as strengthening Washington’s long-term strategic interests in Ukraine. Announcing the resignation, Zelenskyy said Ukraine was “changing its political strategy” and revealed that he had offered Svyrydenko responsibility for “a new, important area” involving relations with one of Kyiv’s key international partners. Outlining the planned changes, the Ukrainian president said experienced officials would be assigned to oversee major foreign policy priorities. “Each priority area of foreign policy will be assigned to a specific person with substantial exp","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 20:27:04 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/ukraine-pm-yulia-svyrydenko-resigns-as-zelenskyy-unveils-major-government-reshuffle-14030849.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"14 nations reject China's South China Sea claims, reaffirm 2016 tribunal ruling","14 nations reject China's South China Sea claims, reaffirm 2016 tribunal ruling","14 nations reject China's South China Sea claims, reaffirm 2016 tribunal ruling The United States, Japan, the Philippines and 11 other countries on Sunday reaffirmed that China's expansive maritime claims in the South China Sea have no legal basis under international law The United States, Japan, the Philippines and 11 other countries on Sunday reaffirmed that China’s expansive maritime claims in the South China Sea have no legal basis under international law. The statement came on the 10th anniversary of a landmark international arbitration ruling that Beijing continues to reject. In a joint statement, the 14 countries described the 2016 ruling by the Permanent Court of Arbitration in The Hague as a significant milestone and said it remains “final, legally binding and definitive” between China and the Philippines. China, however, dismissed the ruling once again, calling it “null and void” and insisting that it neither accepts nor recognises the tribunal’s decision. The joint statement was issued by the United States, the Philippines, Japan, Australia, the United Kingdom, Canada, Germany, Italy, Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, New Zealand, Romania and Slovenia. The countries reaffirmed that there is no legal basis for China’s broad maritime claims in the South China Sea, including those based on what Beijing describes as “historic rights.” The statement also expressed strong opposition to unilateral actions, coercion and the use of force that threaten peace and stability in the disputed waters. It called for freedom of navigation in accordance with the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS). Separately, the 27-member European Union issued its own statement, describing the 2016 arbitration ruling as a landmark decision for the pe","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:41:01 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/14-nations-reject-chinas-south-china-sea-claims-reaffirm-2016-tribunal-ruling-14030846.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,'Traffic is flowing': US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' amid Iran's closure claim,'Traffic is flowing': US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' amid Iran's closure claim,"'Traffic is flowing': US says Strait of Hormuz 'open to all' amid Iran's closure claim US Central Command (CentCom) said maritime traffic is continuing through the strait and that American forces are prepared to ensure freedom of navigation amid escalating tensions between Washington and Tehran. The United States has said the Strait of Hormuz remains open to commercial shipping despite Iran’s announcement that it had closed the strategic waterway following the latest escalation in hostilities. US Central Command (CentCom) said American forces were positioned to ensure freedom of navigation through the vital maritime route. Hours after Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) declared that the Strait of Hormuz had been closed “until further notice,” CentCom said the international waterway remained accessible to all vessels travelling lawfully through the region. “Iran does not control the international waterway used by commercial vessels to globally transport goods and energy,” CentCom said in a post on X. The command added that maritime traffic was continuing through the strait and that US forces were prepared to safeguard shipping despite what it described as Iranian “aggression, harassment, threats, and arbitrary declarations.” According to CentCom, US forces have facilitated the safe transit of more than 800 ships carrying over 400 million barrels of crude oil during the past two months. It also said more than 140 vessels had passed through the Strait of Hormuz in the last seven days. Separately, the Joint Maritime Information Center reported that the southern shipping lane near Oman’s coast remained open despite Iran’s announcement. The latest developments came after US forces carried out another round of strikes on Iranian targets on Sunday, marking the t","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:07:47 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/traffic-is-flowing-us-says-strait-of-hormuz-open-to-all-amid-irans-closure-claim-14030844.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Vietnam boat tragedy: Police detain captain, repatriation of 15 Indian victims begins","Vietnam boat tragedy: Police detain captain, repatriation of 15 Indian victims begins","Vietnam boat tragedy: Police detain captain, repatriation of 15 Indian victims begins Vietnamese police have detained the captain of the speedboat that capsized off the country's southern coast, killing 15 Indian tourists, as the Indian Embassy began the process of bringing the victims' bodies back home Vietnamese police have detained the captain of the speedboat that capsized off the country’s southern coast, killing 15 Indian tourists, as the Indian Embassy began the process of bringing the victims’ bodies back home. The captain, identified as 57-year-old Nguyen Hong Hai, is being investigated for alleged violations of inland waterway transport safety regulations, according to Vietnamese state media. Theaccident occurred on Saturdaynear Phu Quoc, Vietnam’s largest island and one of its most popular tourist destinations. The speedboat was carrying 32 Indian tourists and four Vietnamese crew members when it overturned less than 500 metres from the shore shortly after departing Hon May Rut Ngoai island while returning from an island excursion. The Indian Embassy in Hanoi said on Sunday that the repatriation of the 15 deceased Indian nationals had begun. In a post on social media platform X, the embassy said the mortal remains were being transported to Ho Chi Minh City, where the necessary formalities would be completed before they are flown to India at the earliest. The mortal remains of the 15 Indian nationals who tragically passed away in yesterday’s boat accident are being transported to Ho Chi Minh City and will reach there by this evening.After completion of formalities at Ho Chi Minh the mortal remains would be transported to India… The embassy said its officials, along with the Consulate team, were closely coordinating with Vietnamese authorities, who had assured full ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:01:30 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/vietnam-boat-tragedy-police-detain-captain-repatriation-of-15-indian-victims-begins-14030842.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Iran adviser says Hormuz 'more important than dozens of atomic bombs' amid US tensions,Iran adviser says Hormuz 'more important than dozens of atomic bombs' amid US tensions,"Iran adviser says Hormuz 'more important than dozens of atomic bombs' amid US tensions An adviser to Iran's Supreme Leader, Mojtaba Khamenei, has described the Strait of Hormuz as more important than ""dozens of atomic bombs,"" calling the strategic waterway a key pillar of Iran's deterrence strategy. An adviser to Iran’s Supreme Leader has described the Strait of Hormuz as one of the country’s most powerful strategic assets, saying it is “more important than dozens of atomic bombs” as tensions with the United States continue to escalate. Mohsen Rezaee, a former commander of the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) and adviser to Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, said Iran would continue to defend the vital shipping route, which Tehran views as a key pillar of its deterrence strategy. “This strategic passage is more important than dozens of atomic bombs, and the Islamic Republic of Iran will protect it,” Rezaee was quoted as saying by Iran’s ISNA news agency. According to Iran’s Tasnim news agency, Rezaee said the Strait of Hormuz is a crucial component of the country’s defence strategy and plays a decisive role in protecting Iran’s security and national interests. “The Strait of Hormuz is one of the components of the country’s deterrence and plays a decisive role in ensuring security and national interests,” he said. Rezaee’s remarks came after the Iranian military said the Strait of Hormuz would remain closed “until further notice” following the latest round of hostilities with the United States. The Strait of Hormuz connects the Persian Gulf with the Gulf of Oman and the Arabian Sea and carries nearly one-fifth of the world’s seaborne oil trade. Any disruption to traffic through the narrow waterway can have an immediate impact on global energy markets, with renewed c","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:32:21 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-adviser-says-hormuz-more-important-than-dozens-of-atomic-bombs-amid-us-tensions-14030831.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Iran newspaper lists Trump, European leaders as revenge targets","Iran newspaper lists Trump, European leaders as revenge targets","Iran newspaper lists Trump, European leaders as revenge targets A hardline Iranian newspaper publishes an alleged target list while Tehran steps up military and diplomatic retaliation following the latest US strikes. A conservative Iranian newspaper known for its hardline rhetoric has published a list of individuals it said should be targeted in retaliation for the killing of Iran’s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei. The list reportedly includes the leaders of the United States, Israel and several European nations. In his first public message since the funeral held earlier this week, Mojtaba Khamenei declared on Saturday that retaliation was inevitable. “Vengeance is the will of our nation and must inevitably be carried out.” He also warned that those identified as responsible would not escape the consequences. “These criminals, whose names appear on a list, will take to their graves the wish of a peaceful death in their beds.” TheHamshahrinewspaper, which is published by authorities in the Iranian capital, released an infographic online late Saturday featuring photos of 13 foreign leaders alongside Mojtaba’s statement. The supreme leader in his message said Iran had compiled a list of individuals to be targeted, but did not offer names, and there was no suggestion the newspaper’s list was officially endorsed. The infographic includes US President Donald Trump, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and British Prime Minister Keir Starmer, among others. Khamenei was killed on February 28, the opening day of the West Asia conflict, during joint US-Israeli strikes. His son and successor, Mojtaba Khamenei, has since vowed to avenge his father’s death. As tensions mounted, Iranian Parl","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:32:03 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-names-trump-european-leaders-as-revenge-targets-announces-hormuz-closure-14030820.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,White House ‘will no longer be safe’: Iranian lawmaker warns Trump over Khamenei killing,White House ‘will no longer be safe’: Iranian lawmaker warns Trump over Khamenei killing,"White House ‘will no longer be safe’: Iranian lawmaker warns Trump over Khamenei killing An Iranian lawmaker has warned that the White House “will no longer be safe” for US President Donald Trump as tensions between Tehran and Washington continue to rise An Iranian lawmaker has warned that the White House “will no longer be safe” for US President Donald Trump as tensions between Tehran and Washington continue to rise. According to a report byIran International, Alaeddin Boroujerdi, a member of Iran’s parliament National Security Committee, said revenge for Ali Khamenei’s death had become “an obligation” for his followers and “all free people around the world.” He also warned that Trump, Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and their allies should expect “divine revenge”. The remarks come days after Iran’s current Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei vowed to avenge the killing of his father, who died in joint US-Israeli airstrikes on February 28. Boroujerdi said retaliation against the United States and Israel had now become “a global movement” rather than a “limited response.” He added that “no place in the world, not even the White House, will be safe” for Trump and Netanyahu. The Iranian lawmaker also urged Washington to abandon what he called “impulsive policies” and adopt a more rational approach toward Tehran. According to Boroujerdi, relying on threats and military force would eventually lead to failure for the United States and impose heavy costs on Washington. His comments are among the strongest public threats issued by an Iranian official since the death of Ali Khamenei, which sharply escalated tensions in the region. The warning from Boroujerdi follows recent remarks by Iran’s new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:56:49 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/white-house-will-no-longer-be-safe-iranian-lawmaker-warns-trump-over-khamenei-killing-14030832.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Was Lindsey Graham poisoned? Why Iran and Russia are at the centre of conspiracy theories,Was Lindsey Graham poisoned? Why Iran and Russia are at the centre of conspiracy theories,"Was Lindsey Graham poisoned? Why Iran and Russia are at the centre of conspiracy theories The sudden death of US Senator Lindsey Graham has triggered a wave of unverified international conspiracy theories pointing fingers at Moscow and Tehran, even as allies and world leaders remember him as a leading advocate of Nato, Ukraine and Israel. The sudden and unexpected death of veteran US Senator Lindsey Graham has sparked a flood of online conspiracy theories, with Iran and Russia becoming the focus of unverified speculation. Although officials said the South Carolina Republican died following a “brief and sudden illness,” no evidence has emerged linking any foreign actor to his death. Yet Graham’s recent Ukraine visit, his push for fresh sanctions on Russia, his long-standing advocacy of a hardline policy against Iran and reports of recent threats from Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps have prompted social media users and commentators to question whether there is more to the story. While the Russian angle dominates Eastern European discourse, a second, equally virulent wave of conspiracy theories points squarely at Iran. Graham was arguably the most vociferous anti-Iran hawk on Capitol Hill. He spent decades advocating for the total isolation of Tehran, consistently pushed for military action to dismantle its ballistic missile and nuclear programmes, and loudly cheered the Trump administration’s strikes on Iranian nuclear sites. 5 days ago, Senator Lindsey Graham posted about how the IRGC threatened to assassinate him. They threatened to assassinate me and President Trump as well with matching posters of our faces held by IRGC operatives at Khameini’s funeral that called for our heads to roll.Now,…https://t.co/nOhswRJG6I Iranian state television announced Graham’s death in openly celebratory language, desc","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:03:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/was-lindsey-graham-poisoned-why-iran-and-russia-are-at-the-centre-of-conspiracy-theories-14030816.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Ukrainian drone attacks hit Russia's Samara: One killed, oil refinery targeted","Ukrainian drone attacks hit Russia's Samara: One killed, oil refinery targeted","Ukrainian drone attacks hit Russia's Samara: One killed, oil refinery targeted Kyiv said it had targeted a major oil refinery as part of its campaign to disrupt Russia's energy infrastructure, while a separate drone strike also hit a tanker in the Azov-Black Sea Canal. One person was killed and three others, including a child, were injured after Ukrainian drone attacks struck Russia’s Samara region and targeted a tanker in the Azov-Black Sea Canal on Sunday, according to Russian officials. Ukraine later said that it had targeted an oil refinery in the region as part of its campaign against Russia’s energy infrastructure. Samara Governor Vyacheslav Fedorishchev said the attack damaged residential houses, apartment buildings and an unspecified industrial facility. One person was killed, while three others, including a child, sustained injuries. Russian media reported that the intended target was the Syzran Oil Refinery, operated by state-owned energy company Rosneft. Images circulated by local outlets appeared to show thick black smoke billowing from the refinery, located around 800 kilometres from the Ukrainian border. The facility has been targeted multiple times since the war began. Ukraine’s military later confirmed carrying out the overnight strike on the refinery, saying the attack formed part of its broader strategy to weaken Russia’s energy sector and reduce revenues used to fund Moscow’s war effort. In a separate incident, a Ukrainian drone struck an empty tanker entering the Azov-Black Sea Canal, according to Rostov region Governor Yury Slyusar. Slyusar said the impact sparked a fire that was quickly extinguished. He added that there was no risk of an oil spill because the vessel was not carrying cargo and confirmed that no casualti","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:06:45 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/ukrainian-drone-attacks-hit-russias-samara-one-killed-oil-refinery-targeted-14030819.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US-Iran tensions spiral as Hormuz becomes flashpoint; expert warns peace deal is being ignored,US-Iran tensions spiral as Hormuz becomes flashpoint; expert warns peace deal is being ignored,"US-Iran tensions spiral as Hormuz becomes flashpoint; expert warns peace deal is being ignored Fresh US strikes on Iran following an attack in the Strait of Hormuz have intensified regional tensions, with an expert claiming Washington has abandoned its peace framework, triggering wider retaliation across the Gulf. The fragile US-Iran peace framework came under fresh scrutiny on Saturday after the United States launched a third round of strikes on Iran in response to an attack on a container ship in the Strait of Hormuz, prompting Tehran to retaliate with missile attacks targeting Gulf Arab states. As the confrontation spilled beyond direct US-Iran hostilities, experts said Washington’s failure to honour the peace framework with Tehran is fuelling maritime attacks, widening regional instability and raising the risk of a prolonged conflict across West Asia. Speaking toANI, political analyst and war journalist Waiel Awwad linked the latest attack on a commercial vessel near Oman to what he described as continued American military escalation against Iran. According to him, the recent developments indicate that diplomatic understandings have given way to renewed confrontation, increasing the likelihood of prolonged instability in one of the world’s most strategically important maritime corridors. “Well, there is another vessel that has been attacked right now and that gives you a clear indication that the Americans are escalating the level of attack on Iran. There is no question of honouring the framework they have signed with the Iranians and that’s why the Iranians are attacking all these ships which are using the other route that the Americans have put. Americans are also violating the instructions given by Iran that any ship should get the consent before passing through the Strait of Ho","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:58:25 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-iran-tensions-spiral-as-hormuz-becomes-flashpoint-expert-warns-peace-deal-is-being-ignored-14030814.html,2026-07-13 01:29:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Typhoon Bavi hits eastern China, nearly 2 million evacuated as heavy rain threat grows","Typhoon Bavi hits eastern China, nearly 2 million evacuated as heavy rain threat grows","Typhoon Bavi hits eastern China, nearly 2 million evacuated as heavy rain threat grows Typhoon Bavi, the strongest storm to hit mainland China this year, battered the country's eastern coast with powerful winds and heavy rain before weakening into a tropical storm on Sunday Typhoon Bavi, the strongest storm to hit mainland China this year, battered the country’s eastern coast with powerful winds and heavy rain before weakening into a tropical storm on Sunday. Despite losing strength after making landfall, weather authorities warned that the massive storm system could continue to bring widespread rainfall and flooding across eastern and northern China over the coming days. According to aReutersreport, authorities evacuated nearly two million people ahead of the storm, most of them from Zhejiang province, as emergency services prepared for flooding, landslides and transport disruptions. The typhoon made its first landfall late Saturday night in Yuhuan city before striking Yueqing in Wenzhou shortly after midnight. The storm has tested China’s disaster response system as several provinces already affected by earlier rains now face another round of heavy downpours. According to the report, Bavi left a trail of destruction across coastal Zhejiang after making landfall. Strong winds uprooted more than 700 trees and brought down hundreds more in Yueqing, while flooding submerged roads and low-lying areas. Emergency teams deployed excavators and chainsaws to clear blocked streets and remove fallen trees. State media also reported landslides in the mountainous northern parts of the city, where large rocks crashed onto roads. Rivers overflowed after continuous rainfall, increasing the risk of flooding in nearby communities. In Yuhuan’s coastal town of Kan","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:23:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/typhoon-bavi-hits-eastern-china-nearly-2-million-evacuated-as-heavy-rain-threat-grows-14030811.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"'Go back to where you were born, Mamdani': Actor Robert Davi slams NYC mayor over city map","'Go back to where you were born, Mamdani': Actor Robert Davi slams NYC mayor over city map","'Go back to where you were born, Mamdani': Actor Robert Davi slams NYC mayor over city map ""Die Hard"" and ""Licence to Kill"" actor Robert Davi has sharply criticised New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani after a city map highlighting immigrant neighbourhoods left out Little Italy, triggering backlash from Italian-American groups “Die Hard” and “Licence to Kill” actor Robert Davi has sharply criticised New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani after a city map highlighting immigrant neighbourhoods left out Little Italy, triggering backlash from Italian-American groups. The controversy began after the “New York City Immigrant Enclaves” map resurfaced on social media earlier this week. Critics pointed out that the map identified 30 immigrant communities across New York City’s five boroughs but omitted Little Italy, as well as several historically Jewish and Irish neighbourhoods. Davi, 75, who was born in Astoria, Queens, posted a video on social media platform X, in which he strongly criticised Mamdani for what he described as disrespecting the city’s Italian-American community. Calling the mayor a “jerk,” Davi said, “I hope every New York Italian American and Irish American spits on you when they see you. I would spit on you if I saw you. Shame on you, you garbage man. Shame on you. Respect the city you’re in and understand the people who helped build it.” Forgive my language but i have had enough of these lying lefty pigs to Zohran Mamdanipic.twitter.com/65iRpPBhtc The actor also spoke about his own family’s immigrant history, saying his grandparents came from Sicily and Naples. “My grandparents came from Sicily and Naples and they taught me, speak the English. This is America. God bless America,” he said. Davi added that his grandfather fought for the United States during World War I and later helped build ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:34:32 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/go-back-to-where-you-were-born-mamdani-actor-robert-davi-slams-nyc-mayor-over-city-map-14030803.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"'My life is so weird': Vance shares perks of being a VP, says not getting ‘too big for my britches’","'My life is so weird': Vance shares perks of being a VP, says not getting ‘too big for my britches’","'My life is so weird': Vance shares perks of being a VP, says not getting ‘too big for my britches’ US Vice President JD Vance said that his lifestyle was “totally transformed” after he took office last year. US Vice President JD Vance said that his lifestyle was “totally transformed” after he took office last year. In an interview with podcaster Mike Rowe this week, Vance noted that he flies on his own plane, never goes to the grocery store and has an “army of people” willing to “cook me my food.” “I still haven’t gotten used to it,” Vance said in the podcast. “My life is so weird.” The remarks from the American vice president came amid a national debate ahead of November’s midterm elections over the sky-rocketing cost of living. The 41-year-old Republican firebrand said that his new life also came with some tensions. “It can become the sort of thing that if you internalise it, you start to be an entitled a–hole,” he said. It is pertinent to note that Vance was raised by grandparents and said his grandmother — whom he calls Mamaw — would want him not to “get too big for my britches.” During the interview, Vance also reflected on the experience of travelling in the vice-presidential motorcade, which he referred to as a “ridiculous spectacle” and “the thing that money can’t buy.” He went on to recall the time when he was in a motorcade in Florida with billionaire Elon Musk on the way to Mar-a-Lago. “Traffic was totally shut down on the route to let the motorcade pass,” Vance said. “And Elon’s like, ‘You know, I can buy a lot,’” Vance remembered. “‘But I can’t buy that.’” However, Vance’s comments drew backlash from some Democrats, with some referring to him as out of touch. “Hardwo","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:47:30 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/my-life-is-so-weird-vance-shares-perks-of-being-a-vp-says-not-getting-too-big-for-my-britches-14030800.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Mojtaba Khamenei's public debut? Iran announces memorial for late Supreme Leader,Mojtaba Khamenei's public debut? Iran announces memorial for late Supreme Leader,"Mojtaba Khamenei's public debut? Iran announces memorial for late Supreme Leader Iran has announced a memorial ceremony for former Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, raising the possibility that his successor, Mojtaba Khamenei, could make his first public appearance since assuming the country's highest office Iran has announced a memorial ceremony for former Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei in Tehran next week, raising the possibility that his successor, Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, could make his first public appearance since assuming the country’s highest office. According to aNews18report, the ceremony will be held on Tuesday, July 23, from 5 pm to 7 pm in Tehran. The notice described the event as a memorial for the “martyred mujahid Imam.” However, Iranian authorities have not confirmed whether Mojtaba Khamenei will personally attend the ceremony. The announcement has attracted attention because Mojtaba Khamenei has remained out of public view since succeeding his father afterAyatollah Ali Khamenei was killedduring joint US-Israeli strikes in late February. Questions over Mojtaba Khamenei’s whereabouts grew afterhe did not appear at his father's funeral, one of the largest mourning ceremonies held in Iran in recent years. Instead, state television showed three of his brothers — Mostafa, Meysam and Masoud Khamenei — leading funeral prayers beside the coffins at Tehran’s Imam Khomeini Grand Mosalla. The coffins of Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, his daughter, son-in-law, daughter-in-law and his 14-month-old granddaughter were placed together inside the sprawling religious complex as thousands of mourners gathered to pay their respects. The absence of the new Supreme Leader from such a significant national event fuelled speculation, as he has not been seen publicly since taking ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:47:05 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/mojtaba-khameneis-public-debut-iran-announces-memorial-for-late-supreme-leader-14030801.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Lindsey Graham: The man who pushed for 500% tariff on India over Russian oil purchases,Lindsey Graham: The man who pushed for 500% tariff on India over Russian oil purchases,"Lindsey Graham: The man who pushed for 500% tariff on India over Russian oil purchases While Republican Senator Lindsey Graham will be remembered for pushing conservative, right-wing ideologies, in India he will be known as the American lawmaker who pushed Trump to impose 500 per cent tariffs on New Delhi for Russian oil purchases. Long-time US Senator from South Carolina and a staunch ally of US President Donald Trump, Lindsey Graham passed away on Saturday due to a sudden illness. While the 71-year-old Republican veteran will be known for pushing conservative, right-wing ideologies, in India he will be known for different reasons. Over the years, Graham has created numerous controversies with his provocative statements. While he supported Trump on most matters, he has broken with the president on some issues, especially foreign policy. The division has become wider between the two Republican firebrands when it comes to the ongoing Russia-Ukraine war. While Trump has gone easy on Russia, often calling the country’s President Vladimir Putin a “dear friend”, Graham has maintained a personality of “Russia hawk”, siding with Ukraine and pressing the Trump administration to impose tougher sanctions on Moscow. This pressure was a bane for India as well. Since the start of the war, New Delhi had been one of the biggest buyers of Russian oil. It was this avenue that Graham had been advocating to block. In February this year, Graham claimed that India has reduced its purchase of Russian oil “dramatically”, advocating for the tariffs imposed by Trump on New Delhi. He referred to the move as a “good example” of how policy measures could influence other countries’ actions. A month before that, Graham lauded Trump for “greenlighting” a bill that the senator had worked on (Graham-Blumenthal sanctions bill), which pr","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:19:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/lindsey-graham-the-man-who-pushed-for-500-tariff-on-india-over-russian-oil-purchases-14030762.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani: The Emir who put Qatar on the world map,Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani: The Emir who put Qatar on the world map,"Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani: The Emir who put Qatar on the world map Hamad remained an influential figure within the royal family even after stepping back from public life. He leaves behind a Qatar unrecognizable from the one he inherited — small in size, but impossible to ignore on the world stage Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, Qatar’s former Emir and the man widely credited with turning a small, sleepy Gulf peninsula into a global power player,has died at the age of 74. Known at home as the “Father Emir,” Hamad ruled Qatar for 18 years, from 1995 to 2013. In that time, he transformed a country of roughly half a million people, most of them foreign workers, into a nation with outsized influence in global diplomacy, energy markets and media — despite its tiny size. Born in Doha in January 1952, Hamad trained at Britain’s Sandhurst military academy before joining the Qatar Armed Forces, where he rose to the rank of Major General. He was named Heir Apparent and Minister of Defence in 1977 and gradually took over the running of the country’s affairs while his father, Sheikh Khalifa bin Hamad Al Thani, remained the nominal ruler. That arrangement ended on June 27, 1995, when Hamad seized power in a bloodless palace coup while his father was vacationing in Switzerland. It wasn’t a violent uprising — it was a calculated transition, years in the making. It was built on loyalty Hamad had cultivated inside the military and among tribal leaders. A counter-coup attempt by his father in 1996 failed, cementing Hamad’s hold on the throne. Under Hamad, Qatar’s economy exploded. According to a report by the Qatari government, during his rule GDP grew more than 24 times, and per-capita income rose roughly sixfold. The turning point was his aggressive push to develop the North Field,","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:40:51 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/sheikh-hamad-bin-khalifa-al-thani-the-emir-who-put-qatar-on-the-world-map-14030791.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Polar bears, chili harvests and more... The most spectacular aerial images","Polar bears, chili harvests and more... The most spectacular aerial images","Polar bears, chili harvests and more... The most spectacular aerial images Thousands of bright red chili peppers being harvested, fasting rituals and more... These are the best images from the second International Aerial Photographer of the Year contest First Published:July 12, 2026, 13:31 IST India condemned the attack on commercial vessel GFS Galaxy off Oman. 10 of 11 Indian nationals were rescued, one remains missing. MEA is coordinating with Omani authorities. India urged de-escalation of regional tensions and an end to attacks on commercial shipping.","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:31:20 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/second-international-aerial-photographer-of-the-year-contest-winners-photogallery-14030447.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Spain wildfire that killed 12 begins to ease as firefighters gain ground,Spain wildfire that killed 12 begins to ease as firefighters gain ground,"Spain wildfire that killed 12 begins to ease as firefighters gain ground Firefighters have begun containing the deadly southern Spain wildfire that killed 12 people as calmer weather helped slow the blaze Firefighters battling a wildfire in southern Spain that killed 12 people started to contain the blaze on Saturday as the hardest-hit village remained deserted, with charred vegetation and blackened homes a grim reminder of the inferno that sent terrified people fleeing from their homes. Around 500 firefighters backed by over 20 water-dropping aircraft were battling the blaze which erupted Thursday in the Gallardos area of the southern region of Andalusia, home to many foreign residents. Calmer winds and higher air humidity levels allowed firefighters to directly attack the flames for the first time, officials said. “The fire has not spread at all today,” Justice Minister Felix Bolanos said at the end of the day after travelling to the area, adding that the burned area remained unchanged at 6,600 hectares. “We have taken advantage of a window of opportunity, with favourable weather conditions in terms of wind and humidity today, to intensify our efforts,” he said, expressing hope the blaze could be brought under control in the coming hours. Officials said the 12 people who died in the fast-moving fire had been trapped in vehicles and as they tried to flee on foot. The majority were foreigners although their identities have not yet been released. “We were absolutely terrified. We could see the flames. It was horrific,” Manoli Ramos, 72, a councillor in the small whitewashed village of Bedar where the victims were found told AFP, adding “it was like hell”. Bedar was virtually a ","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:23:53 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/spain-wildfire-that-killed-12-begins-to-ease-as-firefighters-gain-ground-14030787.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Pakistan urges restraint as US-Iran conflict escalates over Strait of Hormuz,Pakistan urges restraint as US-Iran conflict escalates over Strait of Hormuz,"Pakistan urges restraint as US-Iran conflict escalates over Strait of Hormuz Pakistan has called for dialogue and de-escalation after fresh US-Iran military exchanges intensified tensions in and around the Strait of Hormuz. As tensions between the US and Iran continued to escalate, Pakistan on Sunday urged all sides to exercise restraint and pursue diplomacy to prevent further instability in the region. Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister Ishaq Dar spoke with his Iranian counterpart Abbas Araghchi, during which the two leaders discussed the rapidly evolving regional situation, Pakistan’s foreign ministry said. In a statement, the ministry said the ministers exchanged views on the latest developments, with Dar stressing the need to reduce tensions. He “further underscored that dialogue and diplomacy remain the only viable path to resolving disputes and achieving lasting peace and stability in the region”, the statement said. The diplomatic outreach came as the confrontation between Washington and Tehran intensified. Iran’s Revolutionary Guards said on Sunday they had struck a second vessel in theStrait of Hormuz, accusing it of violating regulations in the strategic waterway. State broadcaster IRIB also reported that the Guards had attacked a US base in Qatar. “A second vessel accused of violating regulations in the Strait of Hormuz has been struck,” the Guards said in a statement carried by IRIB. TheUS military announcedthat it had carried out strikes on approximately 140 Iranian military targets in retaliation for what Washington said was an Iranian attack on another commercial ship in the Strait of Hormuz. In a statement, US Central Command said: “U.S. forces hit approximately 140 Irani","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:20:18 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/pakistan-urges-restraint-as-us-iran-conflict-escalates-over-strait-of-hormuz-ws-e-14030785.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"MEA condemns attack on GFS Galaxy off Oman, says 10 Indians rescued, 1 still missing","MEA condemns attack on GFS Galaxy off Oman, says 10 Indians rescued, 1 still missing","MEA condemns attack on GFS Galaxy off Oman, says 10 Indians rescued, 1 still missing India on Sunday strongly condemned the attack on the commercial vessel GFS Galaxy off the coast of Oman, saying 10 of the 11 Indian nationals on board have been rescued, while one Indian remains missing India on Sunday strongly condemned the attack on the commercial vessel GFS Galaxy off the coast of Oman, saying 10 of the 11 Indian nationals on board have been rescued, while one Indian remains missing. In a statement, the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) said India’s Embassy in Oman is closely monitoring the situation and is coordinating with the Omani authorities as search and rescue efforts continue. The ministry also thanked Oman for its support in the rescue operation. Our statement on the attack on a commercial vessel off the coast of Oman ⬇️🔗https://t.co/JtqdfO6iJ0pic.twitter.com/V6jD6zJOtx The statement came astensions in West Asia continue to risefollowing the attack on the Cyprus-flagged container ship, which the United States has blamed on Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC). The incident was followed by another round of US military strikes on Iranian targets. “We condemn the attack on the commercial vessel GFS Galaxy off the coast of Oman,” the MEA said. It added that of the 11 Indian nationals on board the ship, 10 have been rescued so far, while one Indian national is reportedly missing. “Our Embassy in Oman is closely monitoring the situation and proactively coordinating with the Omani authorities in the ongoing Search and Rescue operation. We thank the Omani authorities for their support,” the ministry said. The MEA did not provide further details about the identity of the missing Indian or the circumstances of the attack. Expressing concern ove","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:00:16 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/mea-condemns-attack-on-gfs-galaxy-off-oman-says-10-indians-rescued-1-still-missing-14030782.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Lindsey Graham, US Senator and Trump loyalist, dies at 71 due to 'sudden illness'","Lindsey Graham, US Senator and Trump loyalist, dies at 71 due to 'sudden illness'","Lindsey Graham, US Senator and Trump loyalist, dies at 71 due to 'sudden illness' Longtime Republican Senator from South Carolina and the strong political ally of US President Donald Trump, Lindsey Graham, has passed away at age 71. Longtime Republican Senator from South Carolina and the strong political ally of US President Donald Trump, Lindsey Graham, has passed away at age 71. His office confirmed that the veteran Republican politician passed away on Saturday night. “On the evening of Saturday, July 11, US Senator Lindsey Graham passed away from a brief and sudden illness,” according to the statement. “Senator Graham’s family appreciates prayers at this time and asks for privacy during this incredibly difficult period.” Graham was first elected to the House of Representatives back in 1994; he became a senator in 2002. Interestingly, he was running for reelection this year. Over the years, Graham has been a staunch ally of Trump on several matters. However, he has broken with the president on some issues, such as foreign policy. “He’s outstanding. He’s been at my side for a long time,” Trump said in a tele-rally for Graham last month, acknowledging that the two men had duelled for the 2016 Republican presidential nomination. “After that fight was over, we were best of friends, and he’s helped me as much as anybody in the Senate.” South Carolina Gov. Henry McMaster (R) issued a statement stating that Graham was “the fiercest of fighters for South Carolina and America — and a loyal and steadfast friend.” It is pertinent to note that under South Carolina law, McMaster can make an immediate appointment to fill Graham’s seat. Graham celebrated his 71st birthday on Thursday. Interestingly, he recently retur","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:55:23 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-republican-senator-lindsey-graham-dies-at-71-due-to-sudden-illness-trump-ally-14030771.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Qatar's former Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani dies at 74,Qatar's former Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani dies at 74,"Qatar's former Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani dies at 74 Former Qatari Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, the leader credited with transforming the small Gulf nation into a major global player in diplomacy, energy and investment, has died at the age of 74 Former Qatari Emir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, the leader credited with transforming the small Gulf nation into a major global player in diplomacy, energy and investment, has died at the age of 74, Qatar’s Amiri Diwan announced on Sunday. “With hearts steadfast in faith in God’s decree and destiny, the Amiri Diwan mourns the great loss to the nation of the late – may God have mercy on him – His Highness the Father Amir Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani, who passed away this morning,” the country’s top government body said in a statement. Sheikh Hamad ruled Qatar for 18 years before voluntarily stepping down in June 2013 and handing power to his son, Sheikh Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani. The peaceful transfer of power was unusual in the Gulf region, where leadership changes have often followed the death or removal of a ruler. Reacting to the former emir’s death, Prime Minister Narendra Modi described him as ‘a visionary leader’, whom he last met in February 2024 during his visit to the Gulf nation. We deeply mourn the passing of Father Amir of State of Qatar, HH Sheikh Hamad bin Khalifa Al Thani. A visionary leader who led Qatar to great levels of development and prosperity, we remember him also as a true friend whom I had the honour of meeting during my last visit to Qatar… Sheikh Hamad came to power in 1995 after peacefully deposing his father, Sheikh Khalifa bin Hamad Al Thani, in a bloodless palace coup. Before becoming emir, he had attended Britain’s Royal Military Acad","Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:43:41 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/qatars-former-emir-sheikh-hamad-bin-khalifa-al-thani-dies-at-74-14030767.html,2026-07-13 01:29:47
